24 Jan 11 03:15 source_control_permissions_requirements.md\\n-rw-r--r--@  1 mattbillock  staff   7372 Jan 14 17:18 status_report_2026-01-14.md\\n-rw-r--r--@  1 mattbillock  staff   2216 Jan 13 19:42 task_recovery_analysis.md\\ndrwxr-xr-x@  3 mattbillock  staff     96 Jan 13 21:25 temp\\n-rw-r--r--@  1 mattbillock  staff   7776 Jan 11 03:16 TERMINOLOGY_DICTIONARY.md\\ndrwxr-xr-x@  3 mattbillock  staff     96 Jan 13 21:24 test_results\\n-rw-r--r--@  1 mattbillock  staff   4059 Jan 14 19:37 test_tasks_m1.md\\n-rw-r--r--@  1 mattbillock  staff   4782 Jan 14 03:10 test_tasks_m2.md\\n-rw-r--r--@  1 mattbillock  staff   2281 Jan 13 21:21 test_tasks_milestone1.md\\n-rw-r--r--@  1 mattbillock  staff   2707 Jan 13 21:19 test_tasks.md\\ndrwxr-xr-x@  3 mattbillock  staff     96 Jan 14 00:44 tests\\ndrwxr-xr-x@  6 mattbillock  staff    192 Jan 13 21:17 tmux_monitoring_dashboard\\n-rw-r--r--@  1 mattbillock  staff  14032 Jan 11 03:38 ui_enhancement_requirements.md\\n-rw-r--r--@  1 mattbillock  staff   7747 Jan 11 02:59 ui_enhancements_requirements.md\\n-rw-r--r--@  1 mattbillock  staff   4287 Jan 11 04:21 ui_files_404_fix_requirements.md\\ndrwxr-xr-x@  9 mattbillock  staff    288 Jan 11 03:18 ui_improvements_2025\\n-rw-r--r--@  1 mattbillock  staff  11704 Jan 14 01:44 ui_whimsical_branding_requirements.md\\n-rw-r--r--@  1 mattbillock  staff  11080 Jan 13 21:00 whimsical_names_integration_requirements.md\\n", "stderr": ""}'}]}, {'role': 'assistant', 'content': [{'type': 'tool_use', 'id': 'toolu_01PqfYFxWF2sxFQpMoB2jjcc', 'name': 'read_file', 'input': {'file_path': '/Users/mattbillock/Development/ai_exploration/ensemble/src/field/ensemble_ui/output/achievements_requirements.md'}}]}, {'role': 'user', 'content': [{'type': 'tool_result', 'tool_use_id': 'toolu_01PqfYFxWF2sxFQpMoB2jjcc', 'content': '{"success": true, "content": "# Achievements System - Requirements Document\\n\\n## Project Overview\\n\\n**Project Name:** achievements_system  \\n**Project ID:** b7960dba  \\n**Created:** 2026-01-14  \\n**Executive Director:** Orchestrating implementation\\n\\n## Vision\\n\\nCreate a humorous Steam-style achievements system that awards different agent classes tongue-in-cheek achievements based on their actions. The system should track agent behavior and award achievements as milestones are reached, adding a playful gamification layer to the ensemble agent system.\\n\\n## Objectives\\n\\n1. **Achievement Definition System**: Create a flexible schema for defining achievements with:\\n   - Achievement name (humorous/creative)\\n   - Description\\n   - Target agent class(es)\\n   - Trigger conditions\\n   - Icon/badge representation\\n   - Rarity tier (common, rare, epic, legendary)\\n\\n2. **Achievement Tracking**: Monitor agent actions and automatically award achievements when conditions are met\\n\\n3. **Achievement Display**: Present awarded achievements in the UI with visual feedback (toast notifications, achievement card displays)\\n\\n4. **Achievement History**: Maintain a persistent record of all achievements earned by agent class\\n\\n5. **Achievement Categories**: Organize achievements by theme:\\n   - Productivity (tasks completed, speed records)\\n   - Comedy (failures, quirky behaviors)\\n   - Milestones (first-time events)\\n   - Streaks (consecutive actions)\\n   - Meta (self-referential humor about being an AI)\\n\\n## Scope\\n\\n### In Scope\\n\\n**Backend Components:**\\n- Achievement data model and schema\\n- Achievement definition storage (JSON/database)\\n- Achievement tracking service that monitors agent activity\\n- Achievement award logic and evaluation engine\\n- API endpoints for:\\n  - Fetching available achievements\\n  - Fetching awarded achievements (by agent class, by project)\\n  - Triggering achievement evaluation\\n  - Achievement statistics\\n\\n**Frontend Components:**\\n- Achievement notification system (toast/banner when earned)\\n- Achievement gallery/showcase view\\n- Achievement progress indicators (for multi-step achievements)\\n- Agent profile page showing earned achievements\\n- Achievement filtering and sorting\\n\\n**Achievement Content:**\\n- 20-30 humorous achievements per major agent class:\\n  - Executive Director\\n  - Development Manager\\n  - System Architect\\n  - Code Writer\\n  - Code Tester\\n  - Bug Fixer\\n  - Documentation Writer\\n- Examples:\\n  - \\"Executive Overreach\\" - Executive Director tries to write code (blocked by permissions)\\n  - \\"Infinite Recursion Champion\\" - Spawned 10 sub-agents in a single task\\n  - \\"Test Whisperer\\" - Code Tester achieves 100% test coverage\\n  - \\"Bug Whisperer\\" - Bug Fixer fixes 50 bugs without creating new ones\\n  - \\"RTFM Generator\\" - Documentation Writer creates docs longer than the code\\n  - \\"Premature Optimization\\" - Code Writer refactors before requirements are clear\\n  - \\"Merge Conflict Survivor\\" - Successfully resolved 10 Git conflicts\\n  - \\"Commit Message Poet\\" - 10 commit messages >100 characters\\n  - \\"TDD Purist\\" - Wrote tests before code 100 times\\n\\n### Out of Scope\\n\\n- User-created custom achievements (Phase 2 feature)\\n- Achievement leaderboards across different ensemble instances\\n- Achievement trading or social features\\n- Blockchain/NFT integration for achievements\\n- Achievements that affect agent behavior or permissions\\n- Multiplayer/competitive achievement mechanics\\n- External platform integration (actual Steam, Discord badges, etc.)\\n\\n## User Personas\\n\\n**Primary User: Developer/Operator**\\n- Monitors ensemble agent activity\\n- Enjoys gamification and humor in development tools\\n- Appreciates insights into agent behavior patterns\\n- Values both functionality and entertainment\\n\\n**Secondary User: Executive Director (Self-Aware AI)**\\n- Tracks performance metrics indirectly through achievements\\n- Gains insight into which agents are most active\\n- Uses achievement patterns to identify optimization opportunities\\n\\n## Features\\n\\n### F1: Achievement Definition System\\n- **Priority:** High\\n- **Description:** JSON-based achievement schema with:\\n  ```json\\n  {\\n    \\"id\\": \\"executive_overreach\\",\\n    \\"name\\": \\"Executive Overreach\\",\\n    \\"description\\": \\"Attempted to write code despite lacking can_write_code permission\\",\\n    \\"agent_class\\": \\"executive_director\\",\\n    \\"category\\": \\"comedy\\",\\n    \\"rarity\\": \\"common\\",\\n    \\"trigger\\": {\\n      \\"event_type\\": \\"permission_denied\\",\\n      \\"action\\": \\"write_code_file\\"\\n    },\\n    \\"icon\\": \\"\\ud83d\\udeab\\ud83d\\udcbb\\",\\n    \\"points\\": 10\\n  }\\n  ```\\n\\n### F2: Real-Time Achievement Tracking\\n- **Priority:** High\\n- **Description:** Service that monitors agent activity logs and evaluates achievement conditions\\n- Integrates with existing activity tracker\\n- Triggers award ceremony when conditions met\\n\\n### F3: Achievement Notification UI\\n- **Priority:** High\\n- **Description:** Toast notification appears when achievement earned\\n- Shows achievement name, description, icon, rarity\\n- Plays subtle animation/sound effect\\n- Links to full achievement details\\n\\n### F4: Achievement Gallery\\n- **Priority:** Medium\\n- **Description:** Dedicated page showing:\\n  - All available achievements (locked/unlocked state)\\n  - Filter by agent class, category, rarity\\n  - Progress bars for multi-step achievements\\n  - Statistics (total earned, completion percentage)\\n\\n### F5: Agent Profile Achievements\\n- **Priority:** Medium\\n- **Description:** Each agent class profile shows:\\n  - Recently earned achievements\\n  - Rarest achievements\\n  - Achievement count and total points\\n  - Links to full gallery filtered by that agent\\n\\n### F6: Achievement Persistence\\n- **Priority:** High\\n- **Description:** Store achievement awards in database/JSON file\\n- Persist across sessions\\n- Track timestamps of when achieved\\n- Support for achievement history/timeline\\n\\n## Technical Constraints\\n\\n1. **Integration:** Must integrate with existing:\\n   - Activity tracking system (`activity_tracker.py`)\\n   - Agent spawn/execution pipeline\\n   - Project tracking system\\n   - Frontend React components\\n\\n2. **Performance:** Achievement evaluation should not slow down agent execution\\n   - Async/background processing\\n   - Batch evaluation where possible\\n\\n3. **Storage:** Use existing storage patterns:\\n   - JSON files in `~/.ensemble/achievements/`\\n   - Or extend existing SQLite/database if present\\n\\n4. **Technology Stack:**\\n   - Backend: Python/FastAPI (existing)\\n   - Frontend: React + TypeScript (existing)\\n   - Storage: JSON or SQLite\\n   - Real-time updates: WebSocket or polling\\n\\n## Success Criteria\\n\\n1. **Functional:**\\n   - \\u2705 20+ achievements defined per major agent class\\n   - \\u2705 Achievements automatically awarded when conditions met\\n   - \\u2705 Notifications appear within 2 seconds of earning\\n   - \\u2705 Achievement history persists across sessions\\n   - \\u2705 Gallery displays all achievements with correct locked/unlocked state\\n\\n2. **User Experience:**\\n   - \\u2705 Achievements are genuinely funny/entertaining\\n   - \\u2705 Notifications are non-intrusive but noticeable\\n   - \\u2705 Achievement progress is clear and motivating\\n   - \\u2705 UI integrates seamlessly with existing interface\\n\\n3. **Technical:**\\n   - \\u2705 No performance degradation in agent execution\\n   - \\u2705 Achievement data persists reliably\\n   - \\u2705 Code follows existing project patterns\\n   - \\u2705 Unit tests cover achievement logic (>80% coverage)\\n   - \\u2705 Integration tests verify end-to-end flow\\n\\n## Assumptions\\n\\n1. **Humor Tone:** Achievements should be lighthearted and self-aware, poking fun at AI/developer culture without being mean-spirited\\n\\n2. **Privacy:** Achievement data is local to the ensemble instance (no external reporting)\\n\\n3. **Extensibility:** System should be designed for easy addition of new achievements in the future\\n\\n4. **Performance:** Existing activity tracking provides sufficient event data for achievement triggers\\n\\n5. **UI Framework:** React frontend exists with component library/patterns to follow\\n\\n6. **Backend API:** FastAPI backend exists with established patterns for new endpoints\\n\\n7. **User Preferences:** Users can disable achievement notifications if desired (settings toggle)\\n\\n## Non-Functional Requirements\\n\\n1. **Maintainability:** Achievement definitions should be easy to add/modify without code changes\\n2. **Testability:** Achievement trigger logic should be unit-testable in isolation\\n3. **Scalability:** System should handle 100+ achievements without performance issues\\n4. **Accessibility:** Achievement UI should be screen-reader friendly\\n5. **Localization:** Initial English-only, but structure should support i18n in future\\n\\n## Risks & Mitigations\\n\\n| Risk | Impact | Mitigation |\\n|------|--------|------------|\\n| Achievement evaluation slows agent execution | High | Use async background processing, batch evaluation |\\n| Activity tracker doesn\'t capture needed events | Medium | Extend activity tracker to emit additional events |\\n| Notification fatigue (too many achievements) | Medium | Implement cooldown periods, configurable frequency |\\n| Achievement definitions become stale/outdated | Low | Regular review process, community suggestions |\\n| Storage conflicts with existing data | Medium | Use isolated namespace/directory for achievements |\\n\\n## Milestones\\n\\n1. **M1: Requirements & Architecture** (Current)\\n   - Requirements document complete\\n   - Architecture design approved\\n   - Achievement content brainstormed\\n\\n2. **M2: Backend Implementation**\\n   - Achievement data model\\n   - Tracking service\\n   - API endpoints\\n   - Integration with activity tracker\\n\\n3. **M3: Frontend Implementation**\\n   - Notification component\\n   - Achievement gallery\\n   - Agent profile integration\\n   - Settings/preferences\\n\\n4. **M4: Content & Testing**\\n   - All achievement definitions created\\n   - Unit tests (>80% coverage)\\n   - Integration tests\\n   - Manual QA\\n\\n5. **M5: Deployment & Documentation**\\n   - User documentation\\n   - Developer documentation (adding new achievements)\\n   - Deployment to production\\n   - Launch celebration achievement \\ud83c\\udf89\\n\\n## Open Questions\\n\\nNone - proceeding with assumptions documented above. Executive Director has made decisive choices for:\\n- Technology stack (existing Python/React)\\n- Storage approach (JSON files in ~/.ensemble/achievements/)\\n- Achievement count (20-30 per agent class)\\n- Notification mechanism (toast notifications)\\n\\n---\\n\\n**Status:** Requirements Complete - Ready for Architecture Phase  \\n**Next Step:** Spawn Development Manager with this requirements document\\n"}'}]}, {'role': 'assistant', 'content': [{'type': 'tool_use', 'id': 'toolu_01Av7TEUkPyK3RBceRtwAab8', 'name': 'project_tracking', 'input': {'action': 'add_note', 'project_id': '6df9d558', 'note': 'Found existing achievements system project. User wants to expand with 100 new achievements in musical competition categories: drum and bugle corps (DCI) and British-style brass bands (NABBA)', 'category': 'general'}}]}, {'role': 'user', 'content': [{'type': 'tool_result', 'tool_use_id': 'toolu_01Av7TEUkPyK3RBceRtwAab8', 'content': '{"success": true, "message": "Added note to project"}'}]}, {'role': 'assistant', 'content': [{'type': 'tool_use', 'id': 'toolu_017wgaZsdBY6hHJCS5n7sryW', 'name': 'write_file', 'input': {'file_path': '/Users/mattbillock/Development/ai_exploration/ensemble/src/field/ensemble_ui/output/requirements.md', 'content': '# Achievement System Expansion - Requirements Document\n\n## Project Overview\n\n**Project Name:** Achievement System Expansion  \n**Project ID:** 6df9d558  \n**Created:** 2026-01-14  \n**Executive Director:** Orchestrating implementation\n\n## Vision\n\nExpand the existing achievements system by adding 100 new achievements organized into two specialized musical competition categories:\n1. **Drum and Bugle Corps (DCI)** - Achievements themed around competitive marching music (dci.org)\n2. **British-Style Brass Bands (NABBA)** - Achievements themed around British brass band competitions in the USA (nabba.org)\n\nThis expansion will add musical sophistication and specialized humor to the existing achievement system while maintaining the tongue-in-cheek style and agent behavior tracking.\n\n## Objectives\n\n1. **New Achievement Categories**: Add two major new categories to the existing system:\n   - DCI (Drum and Bugle Corps) category with 50 achievements\n   - NABBA (British-Style Brass Bands) category with 50 achievements\n\n2. **Musical Theme Integration**: Create achievements that cleverly blend musical competition terminology with software development and AI agent behaviors\n\n3. **Expanded Tracking**: Extend achievement triggers to recognize new patterns in agent behavior that align with musical competition themes\n\n4. **Category Organization**: Enhance the existing achievement system to support better categorization and filtering\n\n## Scope\n\n### In Scope\n\n**New Achievement Categories:**\n\n**DCI (Drum and Bugle Corps) Achievements (50 total):**\n- Performance-based achievements using DCI terminology\n- Corps competition references (Blue Devils, Santa Clara Vanguard, etc.)\n- Musical competition scoring and judging themes\n- Marching and precision execution metaphors\n- Examples:\n  - "Blue Devils Precision" - Executed 100 tasks with zero errors\n  - "Santa Clara Vanguard" - Led the ensemble in successful deployments \n  - "Perfect Score (99.000)" - Achieved maximum test coverage on first try\n  - "Drum Major Leadership" - Successfully coordinated 5+ agents simultaneously\n  - "Championship Season" - Completed 10 projects without major issues\n  - "Finals Night" - Delivered critical project under extreme deadline pressure\n  - "Hornline Excellence" - Code Writer produced bug-free code 25 times in a row\n  - "Drumline Precision" - Test suite executed with perfect timing 50 times\n  - "Color Guard Grace" - Bug Fixer resolved issues with elegant solutions\n  - "Show Design Genius" - System Architect created flawless architecture on first try\n\n**NABBA (British-Style Brass Bands) Achievements (50 total):**\n- British brass band terminology and tradition\n- Contest and competition references\n- Musical ensemble and conductor themes\n- British cultural references and terminology\n- Examples:\n  - "Championship Section" - Achieved highest performance tier in all metrics\n  - "First Section Rising" - Improved from previous performance significantly  \n  - "Contest March Mastery" - Led successful project deployments like a contest march\n  - "Principal Cornet" - Code Writer took lead on most challenging implementations\n  - "Soprano Cornet Brilliance" - Delivered high-quality code with exceptional clarity\n  - "Euphonium Excellence" - Provided steady, reliable performance across all tasks\n  - "Tuba Foundation" - System Architect provided rock-solid system foundations\n  - "Percussion Section" - Test suite provided perfect rhythmic verification\n  - "Conductor\'s Baton" - Executive Director orchestrated flawless multi-agent coordination\n  - "Adjudicator\'s Approval" - Code review received perfect score from Bug Fixer\n\n**Enhanced Achievement System:**\n- Category filtering and organization improvements\n- Musical terminology integration in existing UI\n- Rarity distribution across both new categories (common, rare, epic, legendary)\n- Progressive achievement chains within each musical theme\n\n### Out of Scope\n\n- Modification of existing achievement definitions (maintaining backward compatibility)\n- Audio/sound integration (musical themes remain textual/visual)\n- External integration with actual DCI or NABBA systems\n- Real-time scoring systems mimicking actual competition scoring\n- Geographic or regional achievement variations\n\n## User Personas\n\n**Primary User: Music-Aware Developer/Operator**\n- Appreciates both software development and musical performance culture\n- Enjoys sophisticated humor that bridges technical and artistic domains\n- Values achievements that recognize both precision and creativity\n- Understands competitive music terminology and culture\n\n**Secondary User: General Ensemble User**\n- May not know musical terminology but can appreciate the precision/performance metaphors\n- Benefits from expanded achievement variety and themed categories\n- Enjoys discovering new achievement themes and terminology\n\n## Features\n\n### F1: DCI Achievement Category\n- **Priority:** High\n- **Description:** 50 achievements themed around drum and bugle corps competitions\n- Musical competition terminology (finals, semifinals, championships)\n- Corps-specific references and inside knowledge\n- Performance scoring and judging metaphors\n- Precision and execution themes\n\n### F2: NABBA Achievement Category  \n- **Priority:** High\n- **Description:** 50 achievements themed around British-style brass band competitions\n- British musical terminology and traditions\n- Contest section levels (Championship, First, Second, etc.)\n- Conductor and ensemble leadership themes\n- Traditional brass band instrumentation references\n\n### F3: Enhanced Category Management\n- **Priority:** Medium\n- **Description:** Improve existing achievement system to better support categories\n- Category filtering in achievement gallery\n- Category-based progress tracking\n- Category statistics and completion metrics\n\n### F4: Musical Achievement Chains\n- **Priority:** Medium  \n- **Description:** Progressive achievements within each musical category\n- DCI season progression (audition → rehearsal → competition → finals)\n- NABBA contest preparation progression (section placement → championship level)\n- Multi-tier achievements building on musical themes\n\n### F5: Terminology Integration\n- **Priority:** Low\n- **Description:** Integrate musical terminology throughout UI\n- Category headers with appropriate styling\n- Musical metaphor descriptions and tooltips\n- Contextual help explaining musical references\n\n## Technical Constraints\n\n1. **Backward Compatibility:** Must not modify existing achievement definitions or database schema\n2. **Category System:** Extend existing category system rather than replacing it\n3. **Performance:** 100 new achievements should not impact system performance\n4. **Storage:** Use existing achievement storage patterns and file structures\n5. **UI Integration:** New categories must integrate seamlessly with existing achievement gallery\n\n## Achievement Content Requirements\n\n**DCI Achievements (50 total breakdown):**\n- 15 Common achievements (basic DCI terminology and concepts)\n- 20 Rare achievements (specific corps references and competition details)  \n- 10 Epic achievements (championship-level performance metaphors)\n- 5 Legendary achievements (perfect season/historic performance references)\n\n**NABBA Achievements (50 total breakdown):**\n- 15 Common achievements (basic brass band terminology)\n- 20 Rare achievements (specific contest and section references)\n- 10 Epic achievements (championship section performance)\n- 5 Legendary achievements (perfect contest performance metaphors)\n\n**Quality Standards:**\n- Each achievement must be genuinely humorous and creative\n- Musical terminology must be accurate and respectful\n- Clear connection between agent behavior and musical metaphor\n- Appropriate difficulty/rarity distribution\n- No offensive or exclusionary content\n\n## Success Criteria\n\n1. **Content Quality:**\n   - ✅ 100 new achievements defined (50 DCI + 50 NABBA)\n   - ✅ All achievements follow existing humor and quality standards\n   - ✅ Musical terminology used accurately and respectfully\n   - ✅ Clear trigger conditions defined for each achievement\n\n2. **System Integration:**\n   - ✅ New achievements integrate with existing tracking system\n   - ✅ Category filtering works correctly in achievement gallery\n   - ✅ No performance degradation with expanded achievement count\n   - ✅ Backward compatibility maintained with existing achievements\n\n3. **User Experience:**\n   - ✅ New categories are discoverable and well-organized\n   - ✅ Musical terminology is explained appropriately for general users\n   - ✅ Achievement progression feels rewarding within each category\n   - ✅ No confusion between different achievement categories\n\n## Assumptions\n\n1. **Musical Knowledge:** Achievement creators have sufficient knowledge of DCI and NABBA to create accurate references\n2. **User Interest:** Users will appreciate musical competition themes even without deep musical knowledge\n3. **System Capacity:** Existing achievement system can handle 100 additional achievements without architectural changes\n4. **Content Maintenance:** New achievements will require minimal ongoing maintenance once implemented\n5. **Cultural Sensitivity:** Musical competition references will be respectful and celebratory of these artistic communities\n\n## Milestones\n\n1. **M1: Content Creation** \n   - Research DCI and NABBA terminology and culture\n   - Create 50 DCI achievement definitions\n   - Create 50 NABBA achievement definitions\n   - Review content for accuracy and humor quality\n\n2. **M2: System Integration**\n   - Integrate new achievements into existing system\n   - Test category filtering and organization\n   - Verify backward compatibility\n   - Performance testing with expanded achievement set\n\n3. **M3: Testing & Validation**\n   - Unit tests for new achievement triggers\n   - Integration testing with existing system\n   - User experience testing for new categories\n   - Content review and refinement\n\n4. **M4: Deployment**\n   - Deploy expanded achievement system\n   - Monitor performance and user engagement\n   - Document new achievement categories\n   - Celebrate with special "Grand Finale" achievement\n\n## Open Questions\n\nNone - proceeding with standard implementation approach using existing achievement system patterns and extending with new musical competition categories.\n\n---\n\n**Status:** Requirements Complete - Ready for Implementation  \n**Next Step:** Delegate to Development Manager for content creation and system integration'}}]}, {'role': 'user', 'content': [{'type': 'tool_result', 'tool_use_id': 'toolu_017wgaZsdBY6hHJCS5n7sryW', 'content': '{"success": true, "message": "File written successfully to /Users/mattbillock/Development/ai_exploration/ensemble/src/field/ensemble_ui/output/requirements.md (backup: /Users/mattbillock/.ensemble/backups/src/field/ensemble_ui/output/requirements_20260114_204951.md)", "backup_path": "/Users/mattbillock/.ensemble/backups/src/field/ensemble_ui/output/requirements_20260114_204951.md", "was_overwrite": true}'}]}, {'role': 'assistant', 'content': [{'type': 'tool_use', 'id': 'toolu_014Ny3neY3v3tCXLsY7eyJhB', 'name': 'project_tracking', 'input': {'action': 'add_note', 'project_id': '6df9d558', 'note': 'Requirements complete for achievement expansion. Created comprehensive plan for 100 new achievements across DCI (drum and bugle corps) and NABBA (British-style brass bands) categories.', 'category': 'milestone'}}]}, {'role': 'user', 'content': [{'type': 'tool_result', 'tool_use_id': 'toolu_014Ny3neY3v3tCXLsY7eyJhB', 'content': '{"success": true, "message": "Added note to project"}'}]}, {'role': 'assistant', 'content': [{'type': 'tool_use', 'id': 'toolu_0155BJjHqQsf9WskXDwBtbqj', 'name': 'project_tracking', 'input': {'action': 'add_task', 'project_id': '6df9d558', 'description': 'Create 100 new achievements (50 DCI + 50 NABBA) and integrate with existing achievement system', 'assigned_to': 'development_manager'}}]}, {'role': 'user', 'content': [{'type': 'tool_result', 'tool_use_id': 'too