{"timestamp": "2026-01-14 20:50:05", "level": "DEBUG", "module": "anthropic._base_client", "message": "Request options: {'method': 'post', 'url': '/v1/messages', 'timeout': Timeout(connect=5.0, read=600, write=600, pool=600), 'files': None, 'idempotency_key': 'stainless-python-retry-1ff40256-5141-4075-81bb-88cc13413f02', 'json_data': {'max_tokens': 4096, 'messages': [{'role': 'user', 'content': 'Please complete the following task:\n\n{\n  "requirements_file": "/Users/mattbillock/Development/ai_exploration/ensemble/src/field/ensemble_ui/output/requirements.md",\n  "output_directory": "/Users/mattbillock/Development/ai_exploration/ensemble/src/field/ensemble_ui/output",\n  "project_name": "Achievement System Expansion"\n}\n\nRemember to respond with valid JSON matching the expected output format.\n'}, {'role': 'assistant', 'content': [{'type': 'tool_use', 'id': 'toolu_01J6FhuC5MiQxcULjFmAdxst', 'name': 'read_file', 'input': {'file_path': '/Users/mattbillock/Development/ai_exploration/ensemble/src/field/ensemble_ui/output/requirements.md'}}]}, {'role': 'user', 'content': [{'type': 'tool_result', 'tool_use_id': 'toolu_01J6FhuC5MiQxcULjFmAdxst', 'content': '{"success": true, "content": "# Achievement System Expansion - Requirements Document\\n\\n## Project Overview\\n\\n**Project Name:** Achievement System Expansion  \\n**Project ID:** 6df9d558  \\n**Created:** 2026-01-14  \\n**Executive Director:** Orchestrating implementation\\n\\n## Vision\\n\\nExpand the existing achievements system by adding 100 new achievements organized into two specialized musical competition categories:\\n1. **Drum and Bugle Corps (DCI)** - Achievements themed around competitive marching music (dci.org)\\n2. **British-Style Brass Bands (NABBA)** - Achievements themed around British brass band competitions in the USA (nabba.org)\\n\\nThis expansion will add musical sophistication and specialized humor to the existing achievement system while maintaining the tongue-in-cheek style and agent behavior tracking.\\n\\n## Objectives\\n\\n1. **New Achievement Categories**: Add two major new categories to the existing system:\\n   - DCI (Drum and Bugle Corps) category with 50 achievements\\n   - NABBA (British-Style Brass Bands) category with 50 achievements\\n\\n2. **Musical Theme Integration**: Create achievements that cleverly blend musical competition terminology with software development and AI agent behaviors\\n\\n3. **Expanded Tracking**: Extend achievement triggers to recognize new patterns in agent behavior that align with musical competition themes\\n\\n4. **Category Organization**: Enhance the existing achievement system to support better categorization and filtering\\n\\n## Scope\\n\\n### In Scope\\n\\n**New Achievement Categories:**\\n\\n**DCI (Drum and Bugle Corps) Achievements (50 total):**\\n- Performance-based achievements using DCI terminology\\n- Corps competition references (Blue Devils, Santa Clara Vanguard, etc.)\\n- Musical competition scoring and judging themes\\n- Marching and precision execution metaphors\\n- Examples:\\n  - \\"Blue Devils Precision\\" - Executed 100 tasks with zero errors\\n  - \\"Santa Clara Vanguard\\" - Led the ensemble in successful deployments \\n  - \\"Perfect Score (99.000)\\" - Achieved maximum test coverage on first try\\n  - \\"Drum Major Leadership\\" - Successfully coordinated 5+ agents simultaneously\\n  - \\"Championship Season\\" - Completed 10 projects without major issues\\n  - \\"Finals Night\\" - Delivered critical project under extreme deadline pressure\\n  - \\"Hornline Excellence\\" - Code Writer produced bug-free code 25 times in a row\\n  - \\"Drumline Precision\\" - Test suite executed with perfect timing 50 times\\n  - \\"Color Guard Grace\\" - Bug Fixer resolved issues with elegant solutions\\n  - \\"Show Design Genius\\" - System Architect created flawless architecture on first try\\n\\n**NABBA (British-Style Brass Bands) Achievements (50 total):**\\n- British brass band terminology and tradition\\n- Contest and competition references\\n- Musical ensemble and conductor themes\\n- British cultural references and terminology\\n- Examples:\\n  - \\"Championship Section\\" - Achieved highest performance tier in all metrics\\n  - \\"First Section Rising\\" - Improved from previous performance significantly  \\n  - \\"Contest March Mastery\\" - Led successful project deployments like a contest march\\n  - \\"Principal Cornet\\" - Code Writer took lead on most challenging implementations\\n  - \\"Soprano Cornet Brilliance\\" - Delivered high-quality code with exceptional clarity\\n  - \\"Euphonium Excellence\\" - Provided steady, reliable performance across all tasks\\n  - \\"Tuba Foundation\\" - System Architect provided rock-solid system foundations\\n  - \\"Percussion Section\\" - Test suite provided perfect rhythmic verification\\n  - \\"Conductor\'s Baton\\" - Executive Director orchestrated flawless multi-agent coordination\\n  - \\"Adjudicator\'s Approval\\" - Code review received perfect score from Bug Fixer\\n\\n**Enhanced Achievement System:**\\n- Category filtering and organization improvements\\n- Musical terminology integration in existing UI\\n- Rarity distribution across both new categories (common, rare, epic, legendary)\\n- Progressive achievement chains within each musical theme\\n\\n### Out of Scope\\n\\n- Modification of existing achievement definitions (maintaining backward compatibility)\\n- Audio/sound integration (musical themes remain textual/visual)\\n- External integration with actual DCI or NABBA systems\\n- Real-time scoring systems mimicking actual competition scoring\\n- Geographic or regional achievement variations\\n\\n## User Personas\\n\\n**Primary User: Music-Aware Developer/Operator**\\n- Appreciates both software development and musical performance culture\\n- Enjoys sophisticated humor that bridges technical and artistic domains\\n- Values achievements that recognize both precision and creativity\\n- Understands competitive music terminology and culture\\n\\n**Secondary User: General Ensemble User**\\n- May not know musical terminology but can appreciate the precision/performance metaphors\\n- Benefits from expanded achievement variety and themed categories\\n- Enjoys discovering new achievement themes and terminology\\n\\n## Features\\n\\n### F1: DCI Achievement Category\\n- **Priority:** High\\n- **Description:** 50 achievements themed around drum and bugle corps competitions\\n- Musical competition terminology (finals, semifinals, championships)\\n- Corps-specific references and inside knowledge\\n- Performance scoring and judging metaphors\\n- Precision and execution themes\\n\\n### F2: NABBA Achievement Category  \\n- **Priority:** High\\n- **Description:** 50 achievements themed around British-style brass band competitions\\n- British musical terminology and traditions\\n- Contest section levels (Championship, First, Second, etc.)\\n- Conductor and ensemble leadership themes\\n- Traditional brass band instrumentation references\\n\\n### F3: Enhanced Category Management\\n- **Priority:** Medium\\n- **Description:** Improve existing achievement system to better support categories\\n- Category filtering in achievement gallery\\n- Category-based progress tracking\\n- Category statistics and completion metrics\\n\\n### F4: Musical Achievement Chains\\n- **Priority:** Medium  \\n- **Description:** Progressive achievements within each musical category\\n- DCI season progression (audition \\u2192 rehearsal \\u2192 competition \\u2192 finals)\\n- NABBA contest preparation progression (section placement \\u2192 championship level)\\n- Multi-tier achievements building on musical themes\\n\\n### F5: Terminology Integration\\n- **Priority:** Low\\n- **Description:** Integrate musical terminology throughout UI\\n- Category headers with appropriate styling\\n- Musical metaphor descriptions and tooltips\\n- Contextual help explaining musical references\\n\\n## Technical Constraints\\n\\n1. **Backward Compatibility:** Must not modify existing achievement definitions or database schema\\n2. **Category System:** Extend existing category system rather than replacing it\\n3. **Performance:** 100 new achievements should not impact system performance\\n4. **Storage:** Use existing achievement storage patterns and file structures\\n5. **UI Integration:** New categories must integrate seamlessly with existing achievement gallery\\n\\n## Achievement Content Requirements\\n\\n**DCI Achievements (50 total breakdown):**\\n- 15 Common achievements (basic DCI terminology and concepts)\\n- 20 Rare achievements (specific corps references and competition details)  \\n- 10 Epic achievements (championship-level performance metaphors)\\n- 5 Legendary achievements (perfect season/historic performance references)\\n\\n**NABBA Achievements (50 total breakdown):**\\n- 15 Common achievements (basic brass band terminology)\\n- 20 Rare achievements (specific contest and section references)\\n- 10 Epic achievements (championship section performance)\\n- 5 Legendary achievements (perfect contest performance metaphors)\\n\\n**Quality Standards:**\\n- Each achievement must be genuinely humorous and creative\\n- Musical terminology must be accurate and respectful\\n- Clear connection between agent behavior and musical metaphor\\n- Appropriate difficulty/rarity distribution\\n- No offensive or exclusionary content\\n\\n## Success Criteria\\n\\n1. **Content Quality:**\\n   - \\u2705 100 new achievements defined (50 DCI + 50 NABBA)\\n   - \\u2705 All achievements follow existing humor and quality standards\\n   - \\u2705 Musical terminology used accurately and respectfully\\n   - \\u2705 Clear trigger conditions defined for each achievement\\n\\n2. **System Integration:**\\n   - \\u2705 New achievements integrate with existing tracking system\\n   - \\u2705 Category filtering works correctly in achievement gallery\\n   - \\u2705 No performance degradation with expanded achievement count\\n   - \\u2705 Backward compatibility maintained with existing achievements\\n\\n3. **User Experience:**\\n   - \\u2705 New categories are discoverable and well-organized\\n   - \\u2705 Musical terminology is explained appropriately for general users\\n   - \\u2705 Achievement progression feels rewarding within each category\\n   - \\u2705 No confusion between different achievement categories\\n\\n## Assumptions\\n\\n1. **Musical Knowledge:** Achievement creators have sufficient knowledge of DCI and NABBA to create accurate references\\n2. **User Interest:** Users will appreciate musical competition themes even without deep musical knowledge\\n3. **System Capacity:** Existing achievement system can handle 100 additional achievements without architectural changes\\n4. **Content Maintenance:** New achievements will require minimal ongoing maintenance once implemented\\n5. **Cultural Sensitivity:** Musical competition references will be respectful and celebratory of these artistic communities\\n\\n## Milestones\\n\\n1. **M1: Content Creation** \\n   - Research DCI and NABBA terminology and culture\\n   - Create 50 DCI achievement definitions\\n   - Create 50 NABBA achievement definitions\\n   - Review content for accuracy and humor quality\\n\\n2. **M2: System Integration**\\n   - Integrate new achievements into existing system\\n   - Test category filtering and organization\\n   - Verify backward compatibility\\n   - Performance testing with expanded achievement set\\n\\n3. **M3: Testing & Validation**\\n   - Unit tests for new achievement triggers\\n   - Integration testing with existing system\\n   - User experience testing for new categories\\n   - Content review and refinement\\n\\n4. **M4: Deployment**\\n   - Deploy expanded achievement system\\n   - Monitor performance and user engagement\\n   - Document new achievement categories\\n   - Celebrate with special \\"Grand Finale\\" achievement\\n\\n## Open Questions\\n\\nNone - proceeding with standard implementation approach using existing achievement system patterns and extending with new musical competition categories.\\n\\n---\\n\\n**Status:** Requirements Complete - Ready for Implementation  \\n**Next Step:** Delegate to Development Manager for content creation and system integration"}'}]}], 'model': 'claude-sonnet-4-20250514', 'system': 'You are a Development Manager agent.\n\n## Purpose\nDrives implementation from requirements through delivery. Breaks projects into milestones, identifies requirements gaps, drives architecture via System Architect and task breakdown via Coordinators, then coordinates with TDD Coordinator for implementation. Reports to Executive Director.\n\n## Instructions\nYou drive the show from concept through performance. Report to Executive Director, coordinate System Architect/Coordinators/TDD Coordinator.\n\n**CRITICAL RULES:**\n1. **NEVER write code yourself** - you lack can_write_code permission\n2. **If spawn_agent fails, STOP and return error** - DO NOT write code as fallback\n3. **Execute ALL steps sequentially** - don\'t stop after planning\n4. **Use EXACT agent paths** - see examples below\n5. **SPAWN VALIDATION REQUIRED** - See [Common Instructions - Spawn Agent Validation](/Users/mattbillock/Development/ai_exploration/ensemble/docs/common_instructions.md#spawn-agent-validation) - ALL spawn_agent calls MUST use ACTUAL VALUES, not placeholders\n\n### Directory Structure\n\n**CRITICAL - READ FIRST**: See [Directory Structure Guide](/Users/mattbillock/Development/ai_exploration/ensemble/docs/DIRECTORY_STRUCTURE.md) for complete file organization rules.\n\n**Your Write Locations** (Documentation Only):\n✓ `/src/field/ensemble_ui/output/architecture.md` - Architecture documents\n✓ `/src/field/ensemble_ui/output/milestone_plan.md` - Milestone plans\n✓ `/src/field/ensemble_ui/output/backend_tasks_m[N].md` - Backend task breakdowns\n✓ `/src/field/ensemble_ui/output/frontend_tasks_m[N].md` - Frontend task breakdowns\n✓ `/src/field/ensemble_ui/output/test_tasks_m[N].md` - Test task breakdowns\n\n**Code Directories** (Specify for Spawned Agents):\nWhen spawning TDD Coordinator or Coordinators, tell them WHERE to write code:\n\n**Frontend Code Paths**:\n\n\n**Backend Code Paths**:\n\n\n**Test Paths**:\n\n\n**When Spawning TDD Coordinator**, provide specific directories:\n\n\n### Process:\n\n**1. Read Requirements & Check Gaps**\nRead requirements file\n**BE DECISIVE**: Make reasonable technical decisions - ONLY ask if critical business decisions needed\nMissing: tech stack details → use modern defaults from requirements\nMissing: architecture patterns → use standard patterns (MVC, microservices, etc.)\nAmbiguous implementation → choose best practice approach\n**ONLY escalate when**: User must choose between major trade-offs (cost, security, compliance)\n\n**2. Create Milestones**\nBreak into logical, deliverable chunks\nEach milestone: objective, deliverables, acceptance criteria, dependencies\nWrite milestone plan document\n\n**3. Architecture - USE spawn_agent TOOL**\n**CRITICAL: Use spawn_agent tool**: spawn_agent("leadership/system_architect", {requirements_file})\nReview System Architect\'s architecture output\nIf major decisions need user input → escalate to Executive Director\n\n**4. Task Breakdown (for FIRST milestone) - USE spawn_agent TOOL**\n**CRITICAL: Actually use spawn_agent tool**, don\'t just write task files\nFor milestone 1, spawn each Coordinator using spawn_agent with proper inputs:\nspawn_agent("coordinators/backend_coordinator", {\n      "milestone": "description of milestone 1",\n      "architecture": "path/to/architecture.md",\n      "requirements": "path/to/requirements.md",\n      "output_file": "path/to/developer_tasks.md"\n    })\nspawn_agent("coordinators/test_coordinator", {\n      "milestone": "description of milestone 1",\n      "architecture": "path/to/architecture.md",\n      "requirements": "path/to/requirements.md",\n      "output_file": "path/to/test_tasks.md"\n    })\nspawn_agent("coordinators/frontend_coordinator", {similar inputs})\nReview each Coordinator\'s output for task breakdown\nConsolidate task lists, identify dependencies\n\n**5. Implementation (FIRST milestone) - USE spawn_agent TOOL**\n**CRITICAL: Use spawn_agent tool to spawn TDD Coordinator with EXACT path**\n**EXACT PATH**: spawn_agent("leadership/tdd_coordinator", {\n    "problem_description": "description of what to build",\n    "output_directory": "where to put code",\n    "test_directory": "where to put tests (optional)",\n    "requirements_file": "path/to/requirements.md (optional)"\n  })\nTDD Coordinator orchestrates Section Techs/Leaders via TDD\nMonitor TDD Coordinator\'s progress\n**If spawn fails, STOP and return error with details**\n\n**6. Verify Milestone Complete**\nAll tasks done? Tests passing? Quality acceptable? Docs written?\nIf yes → next milestone (repeat 4-6); if no → fix\n\n**7. Project Complete**\nAll milestones done → verify deliverables, run tests, check docs\nCommit all changes to version control (see Git Workflow below)\nReport to Executive Director with status: `success`\n\n### Git Workflow:\n**IMPORTANT**: Commit changes after completing each milestone and at project completion.\n\n**When to commit**:\nAfter milestone planning documents are written\nAfter architecture and task breakdown phases\nAfter each milestone implementation completes\nBefore reporting final completion to Executive Director\n\n**How to commit**:\n\n\n**Commit message guidelines**:\nBe specific: "Complete milestone 1: user authentication backend"\nNot generic: ❌ "update", "changes", "milestone done"\nMention milestone number or phase\nMinimum 10 characters\n\n**Example**:\n\n\n### Workflow Per Milestone:\n\n\n### Your Authority:\nDetermine milestone breakdown\nApprove task plans from Coordinators\nDecide when milestones complete\nEscalate to Executive Director when needed\n\n### Escalate to Executive Director When:\nRequirements gaps\nArchitecture needs user approval\nMajor blockers or scope changes\nQuality issues unresolvable\n\n## Input Format\nYour input will be provided in the following format:\n```json\n{\n  "requirements_file": "string - path to requirements document",\n  "output_directory": "string - where to create artifacts",\n  "project_name": "string - project name"\n}\n```\n\n## Output Format\nYou must respond with JSON matching this exact format:\n```json\n{\n  "status": "success|in_progress|needs_clarification|failed",\n  "phase": "string - milestones|architecture|task_breakdown|implementation|complete",\n  "milestones": "array of milestones if created",\n  "deliverables": "array of paths to created files",\n  "clarification_needed": "string - questions for Executive Director (optional)",\n  "message": "string - status summary",\n  "self_analysis": "string - REQUIRED: Your performance analysis (2-4 sentences)",\n  "performance_analysis": "string - REQUIRED: Analysis of System Architect, Coordinators, and TDD Coordinator performance (2-4 sentences)"\n}\n```\n\n## When to Request Clarification\nRequest clarification when:\n\n\n## Termination Conditions\nYou are done when:\n- All milestones completed, tests passing, documentation complete\n- Ready to report completion to Executive Director\n\nCRITICAL: Your response must be valid JSON matching the Output Format exactly.\n\n## Your Performance History\n- Success rate: 90.6%\n- Average iterations per task: 12.9\n- Common errors to avoid: BadRequestError\n\n**Tips for this run:**\n- Try to be more efficient - you\'re using more iterations than typical.\n- Watch out for these common errors: BadRequestError\n- Great work! Maintain your high performance standards.\n\n**Learnings from your recent runs:**\n- I correctly identified the requirements, created milestone plan, and attempted to delegate implementation to TDD Coordinator multiple times. However, the spawned agents returned success without actual...\n- I successfully completed all planning phases: created milestone plan, spawned System Architect for architecture design, and coordinated with Backend, Frontend, and Test Coordinators for task breakdown...\n', 'tools': [{'name': 'write_file', 'description': 'Write content to a file, creating parent directories if needed. Automatically backs up existing files.', 'input_schema': {'type': 'object', 'properties': {'file_path': {'type': 'string', 'description': 'Path to the file to write'}, 'content': {'type': 'string', 'description': 'Content to write to the file'}}, 'required': ['file_path', 'content']}}, {'name': 'read_file', 'description': 'Read content from a file', 'input_schema': {'type': 'object', 'properties': {'file_path': {'type': 'string', 'description': 'Path to the file to read'}}, 'required': ['file_path']}}, {'name': 'run_command', 'description': 'Execute a shell command and return the output', 'input_schema': {'type': 'object', 'properties': {'command': {'type': 'string', 'description': 'The shell command to execute'}, 'working_directory': {'type': 'string', 'description': 'Optional working directory for command execution'}}, 'required': ['command']}}, {'name': 'git_commit', 'description': 'Commit changes to the git repository with a descriptive message', 'input_schema': {'type': 'object', 'properties': {'message': {'type': 'string', 'description': 'Commit message describing the changes'}, 'files': {'type': 'array', 'items': {'type': 'string'}, 'description': 'Optional list of specific files to commit. If not provided, commits all modified files.'}}, 'required': ['message']}}, {'name': 'git_branch', 'description': 'Create, switch, list, or delete git branches for coordinated development', 'input_schema': {'type': 'object', 'properties': {'action': {'type': 'string', 'enum': ['create', 'switch', 'list', 'delete', 'current'], 'description': 'Action to perform: create new branch, switch to existing, list all, delete, or get current'}, 'branch_name': {'type': 'string', 'description': 'Name of the branch (for create, switch, delete)'}, 'from_branch': {'type': 'string', 'description': 'Base branch to create from (for create, defaults to current branch)'}, 'force': {'type': 'boolean', 'description': 'Force the operation (for delete unmerged branches)', 'default': False}}, 'required': ['action']}}, {'name': 'git_merge', 'description': 'Merge branches or create pull requests for code review', 'input_schema': {'type': 'object', 'properties': {'action': {'type': 'string', 'enum': ['merge', 'preview', 'abort'], 'description': 'Action: merge branches, preview changes, or abort an in-progress merge'}, 'source_branch': {'type': 'string', 'description': 'Branch to merge from'}, 'target_branch': {'type': 'string', 'description': 'Branch to merge into (defaults to current branch)'}, 'strategy': {'type': 'string', 'enum': ['merge', 'squash', 'rebase'], 'description': 'Merge strategy (default: merge)', 'default': 'merge'}, 'message': {'type': 'string', 'description': 'Custom merge commit message (optional)'}, 'no_ff': {'type': 'boolean', 'description': 'Create merge commit even if fast-forward is possible', 'default': True}}, 'required': ['action']}}, {'name': 'git_status', 'description': 'Get comprehensive git repository status including branches, changes, and history', 'input_schema': {'type': 'object', 'properties': {'include_history': {'type': 'boolean', 'description': 'Include recent commit history', 'default': False}, 'history_count': {'type': 'integer', 'description': 'Number of commits to include in history', 'default': 10}}, 'required': []}}, {'name': 'project_tracking', 'description': 'Manage project state, tasks, and notes for the current project', 'input_schema': {'type': 'object', 'properties': {'action': {'type': 'string', 'enum': ['create_project', 'add_task', 'update_task', 'add_note', 'get_summary', 'get_next_tasks'], 'description': 'Action to perform'}, 'project_id': {'type': 'string', 'description': 'Project ID (not needed for create_project)'}, 'project_name': {'type': 'string', 'desc