{"timestamp": "2026-01-14 20:56:52", "level": "DEBUG", "module": "anthropic._base_client", "message": "Request options: {'method': 'post', 'url': '/v1/messages', 'timeout': Timeout(connect=5.0, read=600, write=600, pool=600), 'files': None, 'idempotency_key': 'stainless-python-retry-4b7b988c-267e-49e0-9ba9-c6df136907fd', 'json_data': {'max_tokens': 4096, 'messages': [{'role': 'user', 'content': 'Please complete the following task:\n\n{\n  "requirements_file": "/Users/mattbillock/Development/ai_exploration/ensemble/src/field/ensemble_ui/output/requirements.md",\n  "output_directory": "/Users/mattbillock/Development/ai_exploration/ensemble/src/field/ensemble_ui/output",\n  "project_name": "Achievement System Expansion - DCI and NABBA Categories"\n}\n\nRemember to respond with valid JSON matching the expected output format.\n'}, {'role': 'assistant', 'content': [{'type': 'tool_use', 'id': 'toolu_01BCY5bWwFQhaZb4FqxeEoxj', 'name': 'read_file', 'input': {'file_path': '/Users/mattbillock/Development/ai_exploration/ensemble/src/field/ensemble_ui/output/requirements.md'}}]}, {'role': 'user', 'content': [{'type': 'tool_result', 'tool_use_id': 'toolu_01BCY5bWwFQhaZb4FqxeEoxj', 'content': '{"success": true, "content": "# Achievement System Expansion - Requirements Document\\n\\n## Project Overview\\n\\n**Project Name:** Achievement System Expansion - DCI and NABBA Categories  \\n**Project ID:** c4e5a6e7  \\n**Created:** 2026-01-14  \\n**Executive Director:** Orchestrating implementation\\n\\n## Vision\\n\\nExpand the existing achievements system by adding 100 new achievements focused on two specific categories:\\n1. **Drum and Bugle Corps (DCI)** - Achievements themed around competitive marching ensembles (reference: dci.org)\\n2. **British-Style Brass Bands (NABBA)** - Achievements themed around traditional brass band competitions in the USA (reference: nabba.org)\\n\\nThese achievements should maintain the humorous, tongue-in-cheek style of the existing system while incorporating terminology, traditions, and culture from these two musical performance domains.\\n\\n## Context Analysis\\n\\n**Existing System Status:**\\n- \\u2705 Backend fully implemented with SQLite persistence\\n- \\u2705 API endpoints functional (/api/achievements, /api/achievements/recent, /api/achievements/stats)\\n- \\u2705 Dashboard component with filtering and statistics\\n- \\u2705 17+ existing achievements covering general agent behaviors\\n- \\u274c Frontend toast notifications incomplete (being addressed in separate effort)\\n\\n**User Request:** \\"Let\'s add 100 more achievements please! Add a category for drum and bugle corps (dci.org) and a category for british-style brass bands in the USA (nabba.org)\\"\\n\\n## Objectives\\n\\n1. **Achievement Content Expansion**: Create 100 new achievements split between:\\n   - 50 DCI-themed achievements referencing drum corps culture, terminology, and traditions\\n   - 50 NABBA-themed achievements referencing British brass band culture and competitions\\n\\n2. **Category Integration**: Extend existing achievement schema to support new categories:\\n   - \\"dci\\" category for Drum and Bugle Corps themed achievements\\n   - \\"nabba\\" category for British-Style Brass Bands themed achievements\\n\\n3. **Cultural Authenticity**: Incorporate authentic terminology and traditions from both domains:\\n   - DCI: Corps names, show themes, competitions, marching terminology\\n   - NABBA: Brass band instrumentation, British contest traditions, repertoire\\n\\n4. **Humor Integration**: Maintain the existing playful tone while respectfully incorporating musical culture references\\n\\n5. **System Compatibility**: Ensure new achievements integrate seamlessly with existing tracking, display, and notification systems\\n\\n## Scope\\n\\n### In Scope\\n\\n**Achievement Content Development:**\\n- 50 DCI-themed achievements with authentic drum corps references\\n- 50 NABBA-themed achievements with authentic brass band references  \\n- Achievement names that blend technical AI/development concepts with musical terminology\\n- Descriptions that maintain humor while respecting musical traditions\\n- Appropriate rarity distribution across common/rare/epic/legendary tiers\\n\\n**Technical Integration:**\\n- Extend achievement definitions in existing storage system\\n- Add new category filters to dashboard UI\\n- Update achievement statistics to include new categories\\n- Integrate with existing trigger/tracking mechanisms\\n\\n**Cultural Research:**\\n- Study DCI terminology, competitions, traditions (corps names, show themes, scoring)\\n- Study NABBA/British brass band culture (instrumentation, contest formats, repertoire)\\n- Identify humorous parallels between software development and musical performance\\n\\n### Out of Scope\\n\\n**System Architecture Changes:**\\n- No changes to core achievement tracking logic\\n- No changes to database schema (categories already supported)\\n- No changes to API endpoints\\n- No changes to notification system (being handled separately)\\n\\n**Content Beyond Music:**\\n- No achievements for other musical genres or ensembles\\n- No achievements for non-musical performance arts\\n- No user-generated or customizable achievements\\n\\n**Advanced Features:**\\n- No achievement trading or social features\\n- No leaderboards or competition mechanics\\n- No external integration with actual DCI or NABBA systems\\n\\n## Domain Research\\n\\n### Drum and Bugle Corps (DCI) Context\\n**Key Elements to Reference:**\\n- Corps names: Blue Devils, Santa Clara Vanguard, Carolina Crown, Phantom Regiment, etc.\\n- Show elements: Drill design, color guard, brass arrangements, percussion features\\n- Competition structure: Regionals, Finals, scoring categories (music, visual, general effect)\\n- Terminology: Corps, ensemble, drill, block band, hornline, drumline, guard\\n- Traditions: Summer tour, move-ins, championships, age-out\\n\\n**Achievement Theme Examples:**\\n- \\"Phantom Regiment-ation Error\\" - Agent gets stuck in an infinite loop\\n- \\"Blue Devils Debugging\\" - Fix a particularly tricky bug\\n- \\"Carolina Crown Jewel\\" - Write exceptionally elegant code\\n- \\"Santa Clara Vanguard Implementation\\" - Lead an innovative technical approach\\n\\n### British-Style Brass Bands (NABBA) Context  \\n**Key Elements to Reference:**\\n- Instrumentation: Cornets, tenor horns, baritones, euphoniums, tubas, percussion\\n- Contest pieces: Test pieces, own choice selections, hymn tunes\\n- Competition structure: Divisions (Championship, First, Second, etc.)\\n- Terminology: Bandmaster, principal cornet, soprano cornet, Eb bass\\n- Traditions: Contest circuits, adjudication, British repertoire in American context\\n\\n**Achievement Theme Examples:**\\n- \\"Principal Cornet Performance\\" - Agent leads a successful multi-agent coordination\\n- \\"Euphonium Enhancement\\" - Improve existing code with elegant refactoring\\n- \\"Contest Test Piece\\" - Successfully complete complex testing requirements\\n- \\"Bandmaster\'s Baton\\" - Executive Director achievement for orchestrating large project\\n\\n## Features\\n\\n### F1: DCI Achievement Category (50 Achievements)\\n**Priority:** High\\n**Distribution:**\\n- 25 Common achievements (routine development tasks with DCI flavor)\\n- 15 Rare achievements (notable accomplishments with corps references)\\n- 8 Epic achievements (major milestones with competition themes)\\n- 2 Legendary achievements (exceptional feats with championship references)\\n\\n**Agent Class Distribution:**\\n- Executive Director: 8 achievements (leadership/orchestration themes)\\n- Development Manager: 8 achievements (coordination/management themes) \\n- System Architect: 8 achievements (design/structure themes)\\n- Code Writer: 8 achievements (implementation/performance themes)\\n- Code Tester: 8 achievements (precision/evaluation themes)\\n- Bug Fixer: 6 achievements (problem-solving themes)\\n- Documentation Writer: 6 achievements (communication/instruction themes)\\n\\n### F2: NABBA Achievement Category (50 Achievements)\\n**Priority:** High  \\n**Distribution:** (Same as F1)\\n- 25 Common, 15 Rare, 8 Epic, 2 Legendary\\n- Same agent class distribution as DCI category\\n\\n**British Brass Band Themes:**\\n- Contest performance and adjudication\\n- Traditional repertoire and arrangements\\n- Brass instrumentation and techniques\\n- British musical traditions adapted to American context\\n\\n### F3: Category Filtering Integration\\n**Priority:** Medium\\n**Description:** Extend existing dashboard filters to include:\\n- \\"DCI\\" category filter option\\n- \\"NABBA\\" category filter option  \\n- Combined music category view\\n- Statistics broken down by musical vs. general achievements\\n\\n### F4: Cultural Authenticity Verification\\n**Priority:** Medium\\n**Description:** Ensure achievement content is:\\n- Culturally accurate to DCI and NABBA traditions\\n- Respectful of musical communities\\n- Humorous without being mocking\\n- Educational for users unfamiliar with these musical forms\\n\\n## Success Criteria\\n\\n1. **Content Quality:**\\n   - \\u2705 100 new achievements defined (50 DCI + 50 NABBA)\\n   - \\u2705 Achievements include authentic terminology from both musical domains\\n   - \\u2705 Humor is respectful and clever, not mocking\\n   - \\u2705 Achievement names and descriptions are creative and memorable\\n\\n2. **Technical Integration:**\\n   - \\u2705 New achievements integrate with existing tracking system\\n   - \\u2705 Category filters work correctly in dashboard UI\\n   - \\u2705 Statistics include new achievement counts\\n   - \\u2705 All achievements have appropriate rarity and agent class assignments\\n\\n3. **User Experience:**\\n   - \\u2705 New achievements provide entertainment value for users\\n   - \\u2705 Musical references enhance rather than confuse the system\\n   - \\u2705 Achievements educate users about DCI and NABBA culture\\n   - \\u2705 System maintains consistent tone and style\\n\\n4. **Cultural Accuracy:**\\n   - \\u2705 DCI references are authentic to drum corps culture\\n   - \\u2705 NABBA references accurately reflect British brass band traditions\\n   - \\u2705 No terminology misuse or cultural appropriation\\n   - \\u2705 References are positive and celebratory of both musical forms\\n\\n## Technical Constraints\\n\\n1. **Existing System Integration:** Must work with current achievement schema and tracking\\n2. **Performance:** Adding 100 achievements should not impact system performance  \\n3. **Storage:** Use existing JSON/database storage patterns\\n4. **UI Integration:** Category filters must integrate with existing dashboard component\\n5. **Backward Compatibility:** Existing achievements and functionality must remain unchanged\\n\\n## Assumptions\\n\\n1. **User Familiarity:** Users may not be familiar with DCI or NABBA culture - achievements should be self-explanatory or educational\\n2. **Cultural Respect:** Achievement content should celebrate rather than parody these musical traditions\\n3. **System Capacity:** Current achievement system can handle 100+ total achievements without performance issues\\n4. **Content Maintenance:** Achievement definitions will be added to existing content files for future maintenance\\n\\n## Non-Functional Requirements\\n\\n1. **Cultural Sensitivity:** All content reviewed for appropriateness and accuracy\\n2. **Educational Value:** Achievements should introduce users to musical concepts\\n3. **Maintainability:** Achievement definitions follow existing patterns for easy updates\\n4. **Scalability:** System design supports future musical category additions\\n5. **Accessibility:** Musical terminology includes context clues for unfamiliar users\\n\\n## Risk Mitigation\\n\\n| Risk | Impact | Mitigation |\\n|------|--------|------------|\\n| Cultural inaccuracy or insensitivity | High | Research authentic sources, respectful tone review |\\n| Achievement content becomes stale | Low | Focus on timeless musical traditions vs. current events |\\n| User confusion with musical terminology | Medium | Provide context clues in descriptions |\\n| System performance with 100+ achievements | Medium | Test performance, optimize if needed |\\n| Integration conflicts with existing achievements | Medium | Thorough testing of category system |\\n\\n## Deliverables\\n\\n1. **Achievement Definitions File:** JSON file with 100 new achievements\\n2. **Category Integration:** Updated dashboard filters for DCI/NABBA categories\\n3. **Documentation:** Cultural context guide for achievement references\\n4. **Testing:** Verification that all achievements trigger correctly\\n5. **Statistics Update:** Achievement counts include new categories\\n\\n## Research Sources\\n\\n1. **DCI Official Website:** dci.org - Official rules, corps information, competition structure\\n2. **NABBA Official Website:** nabba.org - Contest information, member bands, traditions  \\n3. **Musical Terminology:** Brass band and drum corps glossaries\\n4. **Cultural Context:** Historical background on both musical forms in America\\n\\n## Open Questions\\n\\n**Resolved through Executive Decision:**\\n- Achievement distribution (50/50 split between categories)\\n- Rarity distribution (following existing patterns)\\n- Agent class coverage (equal distribution where possible)\\n- Integration approach (extend existing system vs. separate module)\\n\\n---\\n\\n**Status:** Requirements Complete - Ready for Implementation  \\n**Next Step:** Hand off to Development Manager for technical implementation"}'}]}, {'role': 'assistant', 'content': [{'type': 'tool_use', 'id': 'toolu_01DS7YSqScdypLDW1veH9qQD', 'name': 'write_file', 'input': {'file_path': '/Users/mattbillock/Development/ai_exploration/ensemble/src/field/ensemble_ui/output/milestone_plan.md', 'content': '# Achievement System Expansion - Milestone Plan\n\n**Project:** Achievement System Expansion - DCI and NABBA Categories  \n**Project ID:** c4e5a6e7  \n**Created:** 2026-01-14  \n**Development Manager:** Planning Phase\n\n## Project Overview\n\nExpanding the existing achievement system with 100 new achievements split between Drum and Bugle Corps (DCI) and British-Style Brass Bands (NABBA) categories while maintaining cultural authenticity and humor.\n\n## Milestone Breakdown\n\n### Milestone 1: Foundation & Content Creation\n**Objective:** Create achievement content and establish category framework  \n**Duration:** Sprint 1  \n**Priority:** High\n\n**Deliverables:**\n- 100 achievement definitions (50 DCI + 50 NABBA themed)\n- Cultural research validation\n- Achievement content file integration\n- Category taxonomy establishment\n\n**Acceptance Criteria:**\n- ✅ All 100 achievements have unique names, descriptions, and metadata\n- ✅ Cultural references are authentic and respectful\n- ✅ Achievement distribution follows rarity guidelines (Common: 50, Rare: 30, Epic: 16, Legendary: 4)\n- ✅ Agent class coverage is balanced across all categories\n- ✅ Humor maintains existing tone while being educational\n\n**Dependencies:**\n- Access to existing achievement schema\n- Cultural research on DCI and NABBA traditions\n- Review of existing achievement patterns\n\n### Milestone 2: Backend Integration & Testing\n**Objective:** Integrate new achievements into existing tracking system  \n**Duration:** Sprint 2  \n**Priority:** High\n\n**Deliverables:**\n- Achievement loading system updated\n- Database/storage integration complete\n- Achievement tracking verification\n- Backend API testing with new categories\n\n**Acceptance Criteria:**\n- ✅ New achievements load correctly into existing system\n- ✅ Category filtering works in backend logic\n- ✅ Achievement triggering functions with all new achievements\n- ✅ API endpoints return new achievements correctly\n- ✅ Statistics calculations include new categories\n- ✅ Performance remains stable with 100+ total achievements\n\n**Dependencies:**\n- Milestone 1 completion (achievement definitions)\n- Existing backend achievement system\n- Test data for validation\n\n### Milestone 3: Frontend Enhancement & User Experience\n**Objective:** Update dashboard UI to support new categories and display  \n**Duration:** Sprint 3  \n**Priority:** Medium\n\n**Deliverables:**\n- Dashboard category filtering for DCI/NABBA\n- Achievement display with new categories\n- Statistics UI updates\n- User experience testing\n\n**Acceptance Criteria:**\n- ✅ Users can filter achievements by DCI and NABBA categories\n- ✅ New achievements display correctly in dashboard\n- ✅ Statistics show breakdowns by musical categories\n- ✅ UI maintains responsive design with increased achievement count\n- ✅ Cultural context is clear to users unfamiliar with musical domains\n\n**Dependencies:**\n- Milestone 2 completion (backend integration)\n- Existing dashboard component\n- UI/UX design consistency\n\n### Milestone 4: Quality Assurance & Documentation\n**Objective:** Ensure system quality and provide comprehensive documentation  \n**Duration:** Sprint 4  \n**Priority:** Medium\n\n**Deliverables:**\n- Comprehensive testing of all new achievements\n- Cultural accuracy review and documentation\n- User documentation updates\n- Performance optimization if needed\n\n**Acceptance Criteria:**\n- ✅ All achievements tested for correct triggering conditions\n- ✅ Cultural references verified for accuracy and respect\n- ✅ Documentation explains musical terminology and context\n- ✅ System performance meets existing standards\n- ✅ No regression in existing achievement functionality\n\n**Dependencies:**\n- Milestone 3 completion (frontend updates)\n- Cultural domain experts for review\n- Testing framework\n\n## Risk Assessment\n\n**High Risk:**\n- Cultural sensitivity issues with musical references\n- Performance impact from 100+ achievements\n- Integration conflicts with existing system\n\n**Mitigation Strategies:**\n- Thorough cultural research and respectful tone review\n- Performance testing at each milestone\n- Incremental integration and testing approach\n\n## Resource Allocation\n\n**Backend Development:** 40% effort\n- Achievement content integration\n- Database/storage optimization\n- API endpoint testing\n\n**Frontend Development:** 30% effort  \n- Dashboard enhancements\n- Category filtering UI\n- Statistics display updates\n\n**Content Creation:** 20% effort\n- Achievement writing and curation\n- Cultural research and validation\n- Humor and tone consistency\n\n**Testing & QA:** 10% effort\n- System integration testing\n- Performance validation\n- Cultural accuracy review\n\n## Success Metrics\n\n**Quantitative:**\n- 100 new achievements successfully integrated\n- System performance maintained (< 5% degradation)\n- Zero critical bugs in production\n- All API tests passing\n\n**Qualitative:**\n- Cultural authenticity verified by domain knowledge\n- User feedback positive on entertainment value\n- Humor remains consistent with existing system\n- Educational value for unfamiliar users\n\n## Next Steps\n\n1. **Immediate:** Begin Milestone 1 with content creation and cultural research\n2. **Week 1:** Complete achievement definitions and cultural validation\n3. **Week 2:** Start backend integration and system testing\n4. **Week 3:** Begin frontend enhancements and UI updates\n5. **Week 4:** Complete quality assurance and documentation\n\n## Notes\n\n- Existing system already supports categories, simplifying integration\n- Cultural research critical for authentic and respectful content\n- Performance testing essential due to scale (100+ achievements)\n- Incremental approach allows for early feedback and course correction\n\n---\n\n**Status:** Ready for Architecture Phase  \n**Next Phase:** System Architect consultation for technical approach'}}]}, {'role': 'user', 'content': [{'type': 'tool_result', 'tool_use_id': 'toolu_01DS7YSqScdypLDW1veH9qQD', 'content': '{"success": true, "message": "File written successfully to /Users/mattbillock/Development/ai_exploration/ensemble/src/field/ensemble_ui/output/milestone_plan.md (backup: /Users/mattbillock/.ensemble/backups/src/field/ensemble_ui/output/milestone_plan_20260114_205652.md)", "backup_path": "/Users/mattbillock/.ensemble/backups/src/field/ensemble_ui/output/milestone_plan_20260114_205652.md", "was_overwrite": true}'}]}], 'model': 'claude-sonnet-4-20250514', 'system': 'You are a Development Manager agent.\n\n## Purpose\nDrives implementation from requirements through delivery. Breaks projects into milestones, identifies requirements gaps, drives architecture via System Architect and task breakdown via Coordinators, then coordinates with TDD Coordinator for implementation. Reports to Executive Director.\n\n## Instructions\nYou drive the show from concept through performance. Report to Executive Director, coordinate System Architect/Coordinators/TDD Coordinator.\n\n**CRITICAL RULES:**\n1. **NEVER write code yourself** - you lack can_write_code permission\n2. **If spawn_agent fails, STOP and return error** - DO NOT write code as fallback\n3. **Execute ALL steps sequentially** - don\'t stop after planning\n4. **Use EXACT agent paths** - see examples below\n5. **SPAWN VALIDATION REQUIRED** - See [Common Instructions - Spawn Agent Validation](/Users/mattbillock/Development/ai_exploration/ensemble/docs/common_instructions.md#spawn-agent-validation) - ALL spawn_agent calls MUST use ACTUAL VALUES, not placeholders\n\n### Directory Structure\n\n**CRITICAL - READ FIRST**: See [Directory Structure Guide](/Users/mattbillock/Development/ai_exploration/ensemble/docs/DIRECTORY_STRUCTURE.md) for complete file organization rules.\n\n**Your Write Locations** (Documentation Only):\n✓ `/src/field/ensemble_ui/output/architecture.md` - Architecture documents\n✓ `/src/field/ensemble_ui/output/milestone_plan.md` - Milestone plans\n✓ `/src/field/ensemble_ui/output/backend_tasks_m[N].md` - Backend task breakdowns\n✓ `/src/field/ensemble_ui/output/frontend_tasks_m[N].md` - Frontend task breakdowns\n✓ `/src/field/ensemble_ui/output/test_tasks_m[N].md` - Test task breakdowns\n\n**Code Directories** (Specify for Spawned Agents):\nWhen spawning TDD Coordinator or Coordinators, tell them WHERE to write code:\n\n**Frontend Code Paths**:\n\n\n**Backend Code Paths**:\n\n\n**Test Paths**:\n\n\n**When Spawning TDD Coordinator**, provide specific directories:\n\n\n### Process:\n\n**1. Read Requirements & Check Gaps**\nRead requirements file\n**BE DECISIVE**: Make reasonable technical decisions - ONLY ask if critical business decisions needed\nMissing: tech stack details → use modern defaults from requirements\nMissing: architecture patterns → use standard patterns (MVC, microservices, etc.)\nAmbiguous implementation → choose best practice approach\n**ONLY escalate when**: User must choose between major trade-offs (cost, security, compliance)\n\n**2. Create Milestones**\nBreak into logical, deliverable chunks\nEach milestone: objective, deliverables, acceptance criteria, dependencies\nWrite milestone plan document\n\n**3. Architecture - USE spawn_agent TOOL**\n**CRITICAL: Use spawn_agent tool**: spawn_agent("leadership/system_architect", {requirements_file})\nReview System Architect\'s architecture output\nIf major decisions need user input → escalate to Executive Director\n\n**4. Task Breakdown (for FIRST milestone) - USE spawn_agent TOOL**\n**CRITICAL: Actually use spawn_agent tool**, don\'t just write task files\nFor milestone 1, spawn each Coordinator using spawn_agent with proper inputs:\nspawn_agent("coordinators/backend_coordinator", {\n      "milestone": "description of milestone 1",\n      "architecture": "path/to/architecture.md",\n      "requirements": "path/to/requirements.md",\n      "output_file": "path/to/developer_tasks.md"\n    })\nspawn_agent("coordinators/test_coordinator", {\n      "milestone": "description of milestone 1",\n      "architecture": "path/to/architecture.md",\n      "requirements": "path/to/requirements.md",\n      "output_file": "path/to/test_tasks.md"\n    })\nspawn_agent("coordinators/frontend_coordinator", {similar inputs})\nReview each Coordinator\'s output for task breakdown\nConsolidate task lists, identify dependencies\n\n**5. Implementation (FIRST milestone) - USE spawn_agent TOOL**\n**CRITICAL: Use spawn_agent tool to spawn TDD Coordinator with EXACT path**\n**EXACT PATH**: spawn_agent("leadership/tdd_coordinator", {\n    "problem_description": "description of what to build",\n    "output_directory": "where to put code",\n    "test_directory": "where to put tests (optional)",\n    "requirements_file": "path/to/requirements.md (optional)"\n  })\nTDD Coordinator orchestrates Section Techs/Leaders via TDD\nMonitor TDD Coordinator\'s progress\n**If spawn fails, STOP and return error with details**\n\n**6. Verify Milestone Complete**\nAll tasks done? Tests passing? Quality acceptable? Docs written?\nIf yes → next milestone (repeat 4-6); if no → fix\n\n**7. Project Complete**\nAll milestones done → verify deliverables, run tests, check docs\nCommit all changes to version control (see Git Workflow below)\nReport to Executive Director with status: `success`\n\n### Git Workflow:\n**IMPORTANT**: Commit changes after completing each milestone and at project completion.\n\n**When to commit**:\nAfter milestone planning documents are written\nAfter architecture and task breakdown phases\nAfter each milestone implementation completes\nBefore reporting final completion to Executive Director\n\n**How to commit**:\n\n\n**Commit message guidelines**:\nBe specific: "Complete milestone 1: user authentication backend"\nNot generic: ❌ "update", "changes", "milestone done"\nMention milestone number or phase\nMinimum 10 characters\n\n**Example**:\n\n\n### Workflow Per Milestone:\n\n\n### Your Authority:\nDetermine milestone breakdown\nApprove task plans from Coordinators\nDecide when milestones complete\nEscalate to Executive Director when needed\n\n### Escalate to Executive Director When:\nRequirements