{"timestamp": "2026-01-14 21:04:01", "level": "DEBUG", "module": "anthropic._base_client", "message": "Request options: {'method': 'post', 'url': '/v1/messages', 'timeout': Timeout(connect=5.0, read=600, write=600, pool=600), 'files': None, 'idempotency_key': 'stainless-python-retry-5911767d-3369-4cc5-8a8f-dc1ce492b937', 'json_data': {'max_tokens': 4096, 'messages': [{'role': 'user', 'content': 'Please complete the following task:\n\n{\n  "requirements_file": "/Users/mattbillock/Development/ai_exploration/ensemble/src/field/ensemble_ui/output/requirements.md",\n  "output_directory": "/Users/mattbillock/Development/ai_exploration/ensemble/src/field/ensemble_ui/output",\n  "project_name": "Achievement System Expansion - DCI and NABBA Categories"\n}\n\nRemember to respond with valid JSON matching the expected output format.\n'}, {'role': 'assistant', 'content': [{'type': 'tool_use', 'id': 'toolu_01BCY5bWwFQhaZb4FqxeEoxj', 'name': 'read_file', 'input': {'file_path': '/Users/mattbillock/Development/ai_exploration/ensemble/src/field/ensemble_ui/output/requirements.md'}}]}, {'role': 'user', 'content': [{'type': 'tool_result', 'tool_use_id': 'toolu_01BCY5bWwFQhaZb4FqxeEoxj', 'content': '{"success": true, "content": "# Achievement System Expansion - Requirements Document\\n\\n## Project Overview\\n\\n**Project Name:** Achievement System Expansion - DCI and NABBA Categories  \\n**Project ID:** c4e5a6e7  \\n**Created:** 2026-01-14  \\n**Executive Director:** Orchestrating implementation\\n\\n## Vision\\n\\nExpand the existing achievements system by adding 100 new achievements focused on two specific categories:\\n1. **Drum and Bugle Corps (DCI)** - Achievements themed around competitive marching ensembles (reference: dci.org)\\n2. **British-Style Brass Bands (NABBA)** - Achievements themed around traditional brass band competitions in the USA (reference: nabba.org)\\n\\nThese achievements should maintain the humorous, tongue-in-cheek style of the existing system while incorporating terminology, traditions, and culture from these two musical performance domains.\\n\\n## Context Analysis\\n\\n**Existing System Status:**\\n- \\u2705 Backend fully implemented with SQLite persistence\\n- \\u2705 API endpoints functional (/api/achievements, /api/achievements/recent, /api/achievements/stats)\\n- \\u2705 Dashboard component with filtering and statistics\\n- \\u2705 17+ existing achievements covering general agent behaviors\\n- \\u274c Frontend toast notifications incomplete (being addressed in separate effort)\\n\\n**User Request:** \\"Let\'s add 100 more achievements please! Add a category for drum and bugle corps (dci.org) and a category for british-style brass bands in the USA (nabba.org)\\"\\n\\n## Objectives\\n\\n1. **Achievement Content Expansion**: Create 100 new achievements split between:\\n   - 50 DCI-themed achievements referencing drum corps culture, terminology, and traditions\\n   - 50 NABBA-themed achievements referencing British brass band culture and competitions\\n\\n2. **Category Integration**: Extend existing achievement schema to support new categories:\\n   - \\"dci\\" category for Drum and Bugle Corps themed achievements\\n   - \\"nabba\\" category for British-Style Brass Bands themed achievements\\n\\n3. **Cultural Authenticity**: Incorporate authentic terminology and traditions from both domains:\\n   - DCI: Corps names, show themes, competitions, marching terminology\\n   - NABBA: Brass band instrumentation, British contest traditions, repertoire\\n\\n4. **Humor Integration**: Maintain the existing playful tone while respectfully incorporating musical culture references\\n\\n5. **System Compatibility**: Ensure new achievements integrate seamlessly with existing tracking, display, and notification systems\\n\\n## Scope\\n\\n### In Scope\\n\\n**Achievement Content Development:**\\n- 50 DCI-themed achievements with authentic drum corps references\\n- 50 NABBA-themed achievements with authentic brass band references  \\n- Achievement names that blend technical AI/development concepts with musical terminology\\n- Descriptions that maintain humor while respecting musical traditions\\n- Appropriate rarity distribution across common/rare/epic/legendary tiers\\n\\n**Technical Integration:**\\n- Extend achievement definitions in existing storage system\\n- Add new category filters to dashboard UI\\n- Update achievement statistics to include new categories\\n- Integrate with existing trigger/tracking mechanisms\\n\\n**Cultural Research:**\\n- Study DCI terminology, competitions, traditions (corps names, show themes, scoring)\\n- Study NABBA/British brass band culture (instrumentation, contest formats, repertoire)\\n- Identify humorous parallels between software development and musical performance\\n\\n### Out of Scope\\n\\n**System Architecture Changes:**\\n- No changes to core achievement tracking logic\\n- No changes to database schema (categories already supported)\\n- No changes to API endpoints\\n- No changes to notification system (being handled separately)\\n\\n**Content Beyond Music:**\\n- No achievements for other musical genres or ensembles\\n- No achievements for non-musical performance arts\\n- No user-generated or customizable achievements\\n\\n**Advanced Features:**\\n- No achievement trading or social features\\n- No leaderboards or competition mechanics\\n- No external integration with actual DCI or NABBA systems\\n\\n## Domain Research\\n\\n### Drum and Bugle Corps (DCI) Context\\n**Key Elements to Reference:**\\n- Corps names: Blue Devils, Santa Clara Vanguard, Carolina Crown, Phantom Regiment, etc.\\n- Show elements: Drill design, color guard, brass arrangements, percussion features\\n- Competition structure: Regionals, Finals, scoring categories (music, visual, general effect)\\n- Terminology: Corps, ensemble, drill, block band, hornline, drumline, guard\\n- Traditions: Summer tour, move-ins, championships, age-out\\n\\n**Achievement Theme Examples:**\\n- \\"Phantom Regiment-ation Error\\" - Agent gets stuck in an infinite loop\\n- \\"Blue Devils Debugging\\" - Fix a particularly tricky bug\\n- \\"Carolina Crown Jewel\\" - Write exceptionally elegant code\\n- \\"Santa Clara Vanguard Implementation\\" - Lead an innovative technical approach\\n\\n### British-Style Brass Bands (NABBA) Context  \\n**Key Elements to Reference:**\\n- Instrumentation: Cornets, tenor horns, baritones, euphoniums, tubas, percussion\\n- Contest pieces: Test pieces, own choice selections, hymn tunes\\n- Competition structure: Divisions (Championship, First, Second, etc.)\\n- Terminology: Bandmaster, principal cornet, soprano cornet, Eb bass\\n- Traditions: Contest circuits, adjudication, British repertoire in American context\\n\\n**Achievement Theme Examples:**\\n- \\"Principal Cornet Performance\\" - Agent leads a successful multi-agent coordination\\n- \\"Euphonium Enhancement\\" - Improve existing code with elegant refactoring\\n- \\"Contest Test Piece\\" - Successfully complete complex testing requirements\\n- \\"Bandmaster\'s Baton\\" - Executive Director achievement for orchestrating large project\\n\\n## Features\\n\\n### F1: DCI Achievement Category (50 Achievements)\\n**Priority:** High\\n**Distribution:**\\n- 25 Common achievements (routine development tasks with DCI flavor)\\n- 15 Rare achievements (notable accomplishments with corps references)\\n- 8 Epic achievements (major milestones with competition themes)\\n- 2 Legendary achievements (exceptional feats with championship references)\\n\\n**Agent Class Distribution:**\\n- Executive Director: 8 achievements (leadership/orchestration themes)\\n- Development Manager: 8 achievements (coordination/management themes) \\n- System Architect: 8 achievements (design/structure themes)\\n- Code Writer: 8 achievements (implementation/performance themes)\\n- Code Tester: 8 achievements (precision/evaluation themes)\\n- Bug Fixer: 6 achievements (problem-solving themes)\\n- Documentation Writer: 6 achievements (communication/instruction themes)\\n\\n### F2: NABBA Achievement Category (50 Achievements)\\n**Priority:** High  \\n**Distribution:** (Same as F1)\\n- 25 Common, 15 Rare, 8 Epic, 2 Legendary\\n- Same agent class distribution as DCI category\\n\\n**British Brass Band Themes:**\\n- Contest performance and adjudication\\n- Traditional repertoire and arrangements\\n- Brass instrumentation and techniques\\n- British musical traditions adapted to American context\\n\\n### F3: Category Filtering Integration\\n**Priority:** Medium\\n**Description:** Extend existing dashboard filters to include:\\n- \\"DCI\\" category filter option\\n- \\"NABBA\\" category filter option  \\n- Combined music category view\\n- Statistics broken down by musical vs. general achievements\\n\\n### F4: Cultural Authenticity Verification\\n**Priority:** Medium\\n**Description:** Ensure achievement content is:\\n- Culturally accurate to DCI and NABBA traditions\\n- Respectful of musical communities\\n- Humorous without being mocking\\n- Educational for users unfamiliar with these musical forms\\n\\n## Success Criteria\\n\\n1. **Content Quality:**\\n   - \\u2705 100 new achievements defined (50 DCI + 50 NABBA)\\n   - \\u2705 Achievements include authentic terminology from both musical domains\\n   - \\u2705 Humor is respectful and clever, not mocking\\n   - \\u2705 Achievement names and descriptions are creative and memorable\\n\\n2. **Technical Integration:**\\n   - \\u2705 New achievements integrate with existing tracking system\\n   - \\u2705 Category filters work correctly in dashboard UI\\n   - \\u2705 Statistics include new achievement counts\\n   - \\u2705 All achievements have appropriate rarity and agent class assignments\\n\\n3. **User Experience:**\\n   - \\u2705 New achievements provide entertainment value for users\\n   - \\u2705 Musical references enhance rather than confuse the system\\n   - \\u2705 Achievements educate users about DCI and NABBA culture\\n   - \\u2705 System maintains consistent tone and style\\n\\n4. **Cultural Accuracy:**\\n   - \\u2705 DCI references are authentic to drum corps culture\\n   - \\u2705 NABBA references accurately reflect British brass band traditions\\n   - \\u2705 No terminology misuse or cultural appropriation\\n   - \\u2705 References are positive and celebratory of both musical forms\\n\\n## Technical Constraints\\n\\n1. **Existing System Integration:** Must work with current achievement schema and tracking\\n2. **Performance:** Adding 100 achievements should not impact system performance  \\n3. **Storage:** Use existing JSON/database storage patterns\\n4. **UI Integration:** Category filters must integrate with existing dashboard component\\n5. **Backward Compatibility:** Existing achievements and functionality must remain unchanged\\n\\n## Assumptions\\n\\n1. **User Familiarity:** Users may not be familiar with DCI or NABBA culture - achievements should be self-explanatory or educational\\n2. **Cultural Respect:** Achievement content should celebrate rather than parody these musical traditions\\n3. **System Capacity:** Current achievement system can handle 100+ total achievements without performance issues\\n4. **Content Maintenance:** Achievement definitions will be added to existing content files for future maintenance\\n\\n## Non-Functional Requirements\\n\\n1. **Cultural Sensitivity:** All content reviewed for appropriateness and accuracy\\n2. **Educational Value:** Achievements should introduce users to musical concepts\\n3. **Maintainability:** Achievement definitions follow existing patterns for easy updates\\n4. **Scalability:** System design supports future musical category additions\\n5. **Accessibility:** Musical terminology includes context clues for unfamiliar users\\n\\n## Risk Mitigation\\n\\n| Risk | Impact | Mitigation |\\n|------|--------|------------|\\n| Cultural inaccuracy or insensitivity | High | Research authentic sources, respectful tone review |\\n| Achievement content becomes stale | Low | Focus on timeless musical traditions vs. current events |\\n| User confusion with musical terminology | Medium | Provide context clues in descriptions |\\n| System performance with 100+ achievements | Medium | Test performance, optimize if needed |\\n| Integration conflicts with existing achievements | Medium | Thorough testing of category system |\\n\\n## Deliverables\\n\\n1. **Achievement Definitions File:** JSON file with 100 new achievements\\n2. **Category Integration:** Updated dashboard filters for DCI/NABBA categories\\n3. **Documentation:** Cultural context guide for achievement references\\n4. **Testing:** Verification that all achievements trigger correctly\\n5. **Statistics Update:** Achievement counts include new categories\\n\\n## Research Sources\\n\\n1. **DCI Official Website:** dci.org - Official rules, corps information, competition structure\\n2. **NABBA Official Website:** nabba.org - Contest information, member bands, traditions  \\n3. **Musical Terminology:** Brass band and drum corps glossaries\\n4. **Cultural Context:** Historical background on both musical forms in America\\n\\n## Open Questions\\n\\n**Resolved through Executive Decision:**\\n- Achievement distribution (50/50 split between categories)\\n- Rarity distribution (following existing patterns)\\n- Agent class coverage (equal distribution where possible)\\n- Integration approach (extend existing system vs. separate module)\\n\\n---\\n\\n**Status:** Requirements Complete - Ready for Implementation  \\n**Next Step:** Hand off to Development Manager for technical implementation"}'}]}, {'role': 'assistant', 'content': [{'type': 'tool_use', 'id': 'toolu_01DS7YSqScdypLDW1veH9qQD', 'name': 'write_file', 'input': {'file_path': '/Users/mattbillock/Development/ai_exploration/ensemble/src/field/ensemble_ui/output/milestone_plan.md', 'content': '# Achievement System Expansion - Milestone Plan\n\n**Project:** Achievement System Expansion - DCI and NABBA Categories  \n**Project ID:** c4e5a6e7  \n**Created:** 2026-01-14  \n**Development Manager:** Planning Phase\n\n## Project Overview\n\nExpanding the existing achievement system with 100 new achievements split between Drum and Bugle Corps (DCI) and British-Style Brass Bands (NABBA) categories while maintaining cultural authenticity and humor.\n\n## Milestone Breakdown\n\n### Milestone 1: Foundation & Content Creation\n**Objective:** Create achievement content and establish category framework  \n**Duration:** Sprint 1  \n**Priority:** High\n\n**Deliverables:**\n- 100 achievement definitions (50 DCI + 50 NABBA themed)\n- Cultural research validation\n- Achievement content file integration\n- Category taxonomy establishment\n\n**Acceptance Criteria:**\n- ✅ All 100 achievements have unique names, descriptions, and metadata\n- ✅ Cultural references are authentic and respectful\n- ✅ Achievement distribution follows rarity guidelines (Common: 50, Rare: 30, Epic: 16, Legendary: 4)\n- ✅ Agent class coverage is balanced across all categories\n- ✅ Humor maintains existing tone while being educational\n\n**Dependencies:**\n- Access to existing achievement schema\n- Cultural research on DCI and NABBA traditions\n- Review of existing achievement patterns\n\n### Milestone 2: Backend Integration & Testing\n**Objective:** Integrate new achievements into existing tracking system  \n**Duration:** Sprint 2  \n**Priority:** High\n\n**Deliverables:**\n- Achievement loading system updated\n- Database/storage integration complete\n- Achievement tracking verification\n- Backend API testing with new categories\n\n**Acceptance Criteria:**\n- ✅ New achievements load correctly into existing system\n- ✅ Category filtering works in backend logic\n- ✅ Achievement triggering functions with all new achievements\n- ✅ API endpoints return new achievements correctly\n- ✅ Statistics calculations include new categories\n- ✅ Performance remains stable with 100+ total achievements\n\n**Dependencies:**\n- Milestone 1 completion (achievement definitions)\n- Existing backend achievement system\n- Test data for validation\n\n### Milestone 3: Frontend Enhancement & User Experience\n**Objective:** Update dashboard UI to support new categories and display  \n**Duration:** Sprint 3  \n**Priority:** Medium\n\n**Deliverables:**\n- Dashboard category filtering for DCI/NABBA\n- Achievement display with new categories\n- Statistics UI updates\n- User experience testing\n\n**Acceptance Criteria:**\n- ✅ Users can filter achievements by DCI and NABBA categories\n- ✅ New achievements display correctly in dashboard\n- ✅ Statistics show breakdowns by musical categories\n- ✅ UI maintains responsive design with increased achievement count\n- ✅ Cultural context is clear to users unfamiliar with musical domains\n\n**Dependencies:**\n- Milestone 2 completion (backend integration)\n- Existing dashboard component\n- UI/UX design consistency\n\n### Milestone 4: Quality Assurance & Documentation\n**Objective:** Ensure system quality and provide comprehensive documentation  \n**Duration:** Sprint 4  \n**Priority:** Medium\n\n**Deliverables:**\n- Comprehensive testing of all new achievements\n- Cultural accuracy review and documentation\n- User documentation updates\n- Performance optimization if needed\n\n**Acceptance Criteria:**\n- ✅ All achievements tested for correct triggering conditions\n- ✅ Cultural references verified for accuracy and respect\n- ✅ Documentation explains musical terminology and context\n- ✅ System performance meets existing standards\n- ✅ No regression in existing achievement functionality\n\n**Dependencies:**\n- Milestone 3 completion (frontend updates)\n- Cultural domain experts for review\n- Testing framework\n\n## Risk Assessment\n\n**High Risk:**\n- Cultural sensitivity issues with musical references\n- Performance impact from 100+ achievements\n- Integration conflicts with existing system\n\n**Mitigation Strategies:**\n- Thorough cultural research and respectful tone review\n- Performance testing at each milestone\n- Incremental integration and testing approach\n\n## Resource Allocation\n\n**Backend Development:** 40% effort\n- Achievement content integration\n- Database/storage optimization\n- API endpoint testing\n\n**Frontend Development:** 30% effort  \n- Dashboard enhancements\n- Category filtering UI\n- Statistics display updates\n\n**Content Creation:** 20% effort\n- Achievement writing and curation\n- Cultural research and validation\n- Humor and tone consistency\n\n**Testing & QA:** 10% effort\n- System integration testing\n- Performance validation\n- Cultural accuracy review\n\n## Success Metrics\n\n**Quantitative:**\n- 100 new achievements successfully integrated\n- System performance maintained (< 5% degradation)\n- Zero critical bugs in production\n- All API tests passing\n\n**Qualitative:**\n- Cultural authenticity verified by domain knowledge\n- User feedback positive on entertainment value\n- Humor remains consistent with existing system\n- Educational value for unfamiliar users\n\n## Next Steps\n\n1. **Immediate:** Begin Milestone 1 with content creation and cultural research\n2. **Week 1:** Complete achievement definitions and cultural validation\n3. **Week 2:** Start backend integration and system testing\n4. **Week 3:** Begin frontend enhancements and UI updates\n5. **Week 4:** Complete quality assurance and documentation\n\n## Notes\n\n- Existing system already supports categories, simplifying integration\n- Cultural research critical for authentic and respectful content\n- Performance testing essential due to scale (100+ achievements)\n- Incremental approach allows for early feedback and course correction\n\n---\n\n**Status:** Ready for Architecture Phase  \n**Next Phase:** System Architect consultation for technical approach'}}]}, {'role': 'user', 'content': [{'type': 'tool_result', 'tool_use_id': 'toolu_01DS7YSqScdypLDW1veH9qQD', 'content': '{"success": true, "message": "File written successfully to /Users/mattbillock/Development/ai_exploration/ensemble/src/field/ensemble_ui/output/milestone_plan.md (backup: /Users/mattbillock/.ensemble/backups/src/field/ensemble_ui/output/milestone_plan_20260114_205652.md)", "backup_path": "/Users/mattbillock/.ensemble/backups/src/field/ensemble_ui/output/milestone_plan_20260114_205652.md", "was_overwrite": true}'}]}, {'role': 'assistant', 'content': [{'type': 'tool_use', 'id': 'toolu_01Fd97vvKT81R7V16dK4hBPU', 'name': 'spawn_agent', 'input': {'agent_type': 'leadership/system_architect', 'input_data': {'requirements_file': '/Users/mattbillock/Development/ai_exploration/ensemble/src/field/ensemble_ui/output/requirements.md', 'output_directory': '/Users/mattbillock/Development/ai_exploration/ensemble/src/field/ensemble_ui/output', 'project_name': 'Achievement System Expansion - DCI and NABBA Categories'}}}]}, {'role': 'user', 'content': [{'type': 'tool_result', 'tool_use_id': 'toolu_01Fd97vvKT81R7V16dK4hBPU', 'content': '{"success": false, "error": "Missing required input field: output_file"}'}]}, {'role': 'assistant', 'content': [{'type': 'tool_use', 'id': 'toolu_01XJ72fxS27553VhuirommvW', 'name': 'spawn_agent', 'input': {'agent_type': 'leadership/system_architect', 'input_data': {'requirements_file': '/Users/mattbillock/Development/ai_exploration/ensemble/src/field/ensemble_ui/output/requirements.md', 'output_file': '/Users/mattbillock/Development/ai_exploration/ensemble/src/field/ensemble_ui/output/architecture.md', 'project_name': 'Achievement System Expansion - DCI and NABBA Categories'}}}]}, {'role': 'user', 'content': [{'type': 'tool_result', 'tool_use_id': 'toolu_01XJ72fxS27553VhuirommvW', 'content': '{"success": true, "result": {"status": "success", "architecture_file": "/Users/mattbillock/Development/ai_exploration/ensemble/src/field/ensemble_ui/output/architecture.md", "message": "Designed a client-side React SPA architecture optimized for instant name generation, family-friendly content, and zero backend dependencies. Uses component-based architecture with TypeScript for type safety and Vite for optimal developer experience.", "key_decisions": ["Client-side only architecture with no backend - all word data is static and generation is computational", "React 18 + TypeScript + Vite stack - provides excellent developer experience and type safety for word pools", "Pure CSS Modules for styling - avoids unnecessary dependencies while maintaining scoped styles", "React hooks only for state management - no Redux/Context needed for simple state requirements", "Static hosting deployment (Netlify/Vercel) - perfect for SPA with no server requirements", "Comprehensive testing strategy with Vitest + React Testing Library - ensures name quality and user experience", "Pre-curated word pools with validation rules - guarantees family-friendly content without runtime filtering"], "self_analysis": "Successfully analyzed a straightforward SPA project and made appropriate architectural choices that match the simple requirements. Avoided over-engineering while still providing a robust, maintainable solution. The decision to keep everything client-side and avoid external dependencies aligns perfectly with the instant-generation performance requirement."}}'}]}, {'role': 'assistant', 'content': [{'type': 'tool_use', 'id': 'toolu_01ToM7HJdiSfMwV33Bz6y25z', 'name': 'read_file', 'input': {'file_path': '/Users/mattbillock/Development/ai_exploration/ensemble/src/field/ensemble_ui/output/architecture.md'}}]}, {'role': 'user', 'content': [{'type': 'tool_result', 'tool_use_id': 'toolu_01ToM7HJdiSfMwV33Bz6y25z', 'content': '{"success": true, "content": "# Whimsical Name Generator - Architecture Proposal\\n\\n## Architecture Overview\\n\\n### High-Level Design\\nThis is a **Single Page Application (SPA)** using a **client-side only architecture**. The application follows a **Component-Based Architecture** pattern with React, emphasizing simplicity, performance, and maintainability.\\n\\n**Architecture Pattern**: Component-Based Architecture with Functional Programming\\n**Deployment Model**: Static Site - can be deployed to any static hosting service\\n**Data Flow**: Unidirectional data flow using React hooks and local state\\n\\n### Rationale\\n- **Client-side only**: No backend needed since all word data is static and name generation is computational\\n- **SPA**: Single purpose application doesn\'t require routing or complex state management\\n- **Component-based**: React\'s component model perfectly fits the modular nature of the UI\\n- **Functional approach**: Name generation is pure function, fits functional paradigm well\\n\\n## Tech Stack\\n\\n### Frontend Framework\\n**React 18+ with TypeScript**\\n- **Why React**: Excellent for component-based UI, great ecosystem, widely known\\n- **Why TypeScript**: Type safety for word pools and generation logic, better developer experience\\n- **Alternatives considered**: Vanilla JS (rejected: harder to maintain), Vue (rejected: React is more widely known for this use case)\\n\\n### Build Tool\\n**Vite**\\n- **Why Vite**: Fast development, excellent TypeScript support, optimized builds\\n- **Why not Create React App**: CRA is slower and has more overhead than needed\\n- **Why not Webpack directly**: Vite provides better developer experience out of the box\\n\\n### Styling\\n**CSS Modules + Modern CSS**\\n- **Why CSS Modules**: Scoped styling without additional complexity\\n- **Why not Styled Components**: Adds unnecessary bundle size for simple styling needs\\n- **Why not Tailwind**: Overkill for simple UI, CSS Modules provide cleaner code\\n\\n### State Management\\n**React Hooks (useState, useCallback)**\\n- **Why React Hooks**: Simple state needs don\'t require external state management\\n- **Why not Redux**: Massive overkill for this simple application\\n- **Why not Context**: No state sharing between distant components needed\\n\\n### Utilities\\n**No external dependencies for core functionality**\\n- Name generation will be pure JavaScript/TypeScript\\n- Copy-to-clipboard using Web APIs\\n- **Why no external libs**: Keeps bundle small, reduces security surface, improves performance\\n\\n## System Components\\n\\n### Component Architecture\\n\\n```\\nApp\\n\\u251c\\u2500\\u2500 Header (title, description)\\n\\u251c\\u2500\\u2500 NameGenerator\\n\\u2502   \\u251c\\u2500\\u2500 NameDisplay\\n\\u2502   \\u251c\\u2500\\u2500 GenerateButton\\n\\u2502   \\u2514\\u2500\\u2500 CopyButton\\n\\u2514\\u2500\\u2500 Footer (credits, info)\\n```\\n\\n### Core Components\\n\\n#### 1. App Component\\n- **Responsibility**: Root component, layout structure\\n- **State**: None (stateless)\\n- **Interactions**: Renders child components\\n\\n#### 2. NameGenerator Component\\n- **Responsibility**: Contains all name generation logic and UI\\n- **State**: `currentName: string | null`, `isGenerating: boolean`\\n- **Interactions**: Manages name generation, coordinates child components\\n\\n#### 3. NameDisplay Component\\n- **Responsibility**: Shows the currently generated name\\n- **Props**: `name: string | null`\\n- **Behavior**: Smooth animations for name changes\\n\\n#### 4. GenerateButton Component\\n- **Responsibility**: Triggers name generation\\n- **Props**: `onGenerate: () => void`, `isGenerating: boolean`\\n- **Behavior**: Handles click events, shows loading state\\n\\n#### 5. CopyButton Component\\n- **Responsibility**: Copies name to clipboard\\n- **Props**: `name: string`, `onCopy: () => void`\\n- **Behavior**: Clipboard API integration, feedback on success\\n\\n### Core Services\\n\\n#### 1. NameGenerator Service\\n```typescript\\ninterface NameGeneratorService {\\n  generateName(): string;\\n}\\n```\\n- **Responsibility**: Pure function that combines words to create names\\n- **Input**: None (uses internal word pools)\\n- **Output**: String containing generated name\\n- **Logic**: Smart combination with rules to avoid awkward phrasing\\n\\n#### 2. WordPool Service\\n```typescript\\ninterface WordPool {\\n  adjectives: string[];\\n  nouns: string[];\\n  descriptors: string[];\\n}\\n```\\n- **Responsibility**: Provides curated word lists\\n- **Content**: 50+ words per category, all family-friendly\\n- **Validation**: All words pre-validated for appropriateness\\n\\n## File/Directory Structure\\n\\n```\\nsrc/\\n\\u251c\\u2500\\u2500 components/\\n\\u2502   \\u251c\\u2500\\u2500 App/\\n\\u2502   \\u2502   \\u251c\\u2500\\u2500 App.tsx\\n\\u2502   \\u2502   \\u251c\\u2500\\u2500 App.module.css\\n\\u2502   \\u2502   \\u2514\\u2500\\u2500 index.ts\\n\\u2502   \\u251c\\u2500\\u2500 NameGenerator/\\n\\u2502   \\u2502   \\u251c\\u2500\\u2500 NameGenerator.tsx\\n\\u2502   \\u2502   \\u251c\\u2500\\u2500 NameGenerator.module.css\\n\\u2502   \\u2502   \\u2514\\u2500\\u2500 index.ts\\n\\u2502   \\u251c\\u2500\\u2500 NameDisplay/\\n\\u2502   \\u2502   \\u251c\\u2500\\u2500 NameDisplay.tsx\\n\\u2502   \\u2502   \\u251c\\u2500\\u2500 NameDisplay.module.css\\n\\u2502   \\u2502   \\u2514\\u2500\\u2500 index.ts\\n\\u2502   \\u251c\\u2500\\u2500 GenerateButton/\\n\\u2502   \\u2502   \\u251c\\u2500\\u2500 GenerateButton.tsx\\n\\u2502   \\u2502   \\u251c\\u2500\\u2500 GenerateButton.module.css\\n\\u2502   \\u2502   \\u2514\\u2500\\u2500 index.ts\\n\\u2502   \\u2514\\u2500\\u2500 CopyButton/\\n\\u2502       \\u251c\\u2500\\u2500 CopyButton.tsx\\n\\u2502       \\u251c\\u2500\\u2500 CopyButton.module.css\\n\\u2502       \\u2514\\u2500\\u2500 index.ts\\n\\u251c\\u2500\\u2500 services/\\n\\u2502   \\u251c\\u2500\\u2500 nameGenerator.ts\\n\\u2502   \\u251c\\u2500\\u2500 wordPools.ts\\n\\u2502   \\u2514\\u2500\\u2500 types.ts\\n\\u251c\\u2500\\u2500 styles/\\n\\u2502   \\u251c\\u2500\\u2500 globals.css\\n\\u2502   \\u2514\\u2500\\u2500 variables.css\\n\\u251c\\u2500\\u2500 utils/\\n\\u2502   \\u251c\\u2500\\u2500 clipboard.ts\\n\\u2502   \\u2514\\u2500\\u2500 randomUtils.ts\\n\\u251c\\u2500\\u2500 __tests__/\\n\\u2502   \\u251c\\u2500\\u2500 components/\\n\\u2502   \\u2514\\u2500\\u2500 services/\\n\\u251c\\u2500\\u2500 main.tsx\\n\\u251c\\u2500\\u2500 index.html\\n\\u2514\\u2500\\u2500 vite.config.ts\\n```\\n\\n### Rationale for Structure\\n- **Component folders**: Each component is self-contained with its styles and index file\\n- **Services separation**: Business logic separated from UI components\\n- **Utils folder**: Reusable utilities that aren\'t business logic\\n- **Tests mirror structure**: Easy to find tests for any component or service\\n\\n## Data Model\\n\\n### Word Pool Structure\\n```typescript\\ninterface WordPool {\\n  adjectives: string[];\\n  nouns: string[];\\n  descriptors: string[];\\n}\\n\\ninterface GeneratedName {\\n  adjective: string;\\n  noun: string;\\n  descriptor: string;\\n  fullName: string;\\n}\\n```\\n\\n### State Structure\\n```typescript\\ninterface NameGeneratorState {\\n  currentName: string | null;\\n  isGenerating: boolean;\\n  copyFeedback: boolean;\\n}\\n```\\n\\n### Data Flow\\n1. User clicks \\"Generate\\" button\\n2. NameGenerator component calls generateName() service\\n3. Service randomly selects words from each pool\\n4. Service combines words using generation rules\\n5. Component updates state with new name\\n6. NameDisplay component re-renders with animation\\n7. User can copy name using CopyButton\\n\\n## API Design\\n\\nThis is a client-side only application, so no REST APIs. However, the internal service interfaces act as our \\"API\\":\\n\\n### Name Generation Service API\\n```typescript\\n// Primary generation function\\ngenerateName(): string\\n\\n// Utility functions\\ngetRandomAdjective(): string\\ngetRandomNoun(): string  \\ngetRandomDescriptor(): string\\ncombineWords(adj: string, noun: string, desc: string): string\\n```\\n\\n### Clipboard Service API\\n```typescript\\ncopyToClipboard(text: string): Promise<boolean>\\n```\\n\\n## Deployment Strategy\\n\\n### Build Process\\n1. **Development**: Vite dev server with hot reload\\n2. **Build**: `vite build` creates optimized production bundle\\n3. **Output**: Static files (HTML, CSS, JS) in `dist/` folder\\n\\n### Deployment Options\\n**Recommended: Netlify or Vercel**\\n- **Why**: Automatic deployments from Git, edge CDN, free tier sufficient\\n- **Setup**: Connect Git repo, auto-deploy on push to main\\n- **Custom domain**: Easy to configure\\n\\n**Alternative Options**:\\n- GitHub Pages (free, but slower builds)\\n- AWS S3 + CloudFront (more complex setup)\\n- Any static hosting service\\n\\n### Environment Configuration\\n```typescript\\n// No environment variables needed - everything is static\\n// Optional: build-time configuration for analytics\\n```\\n\\n### CI/CD Strategy\\n**GitHub Actions Workflow**:\\n1. Run tests on push to any branch\\n2. Run build to verify compilation\\n3. Deploy to staging on push to develop\\n4. Deploy to production on push to main\\n\\n## Testing Strategy\\n\\n### Unit Testing\\n**Framework**: Vitest (Vite\'s native testing solution)\\n- **Why Vitest**: Perfect integration with Vite, fast, Jest-compatible API\\n- **What to test**: \\n  - Word generation logic (pure functions)\\n  - Name combination rules\\n  - Clipboard utility functions\\n\\n### Component Testing\\n**Framework**: React Testing Library with Vitest**\\n- **Why RTL**: Tests component behavior from user perspective\\n- **What to test**:\\n  - Button click handlers\\n  - Name display updates\\n  - Copy functionality\\n  - Accessibility features\\n\\n### Integration Testing\\n**Approach**: Test complete user flows\\n- **Scenarios**:\\n  - Generate name and copy to clipboard\\n  - Multiple name generations show variety\\n  - Error handling for clipboard failures\\n\\n### Content Testing\\n**Approach**: Automated validation of word pools\\n- **Tests**:\\n  - All words are family-friendly (automated screening)\\n  - No duplicate words in pools\\n  - Minimum word count per category\\n  - No potentially offensive combinations\\n\\n### Testing Commands\\n```bash\\nnpm run test          # Run all tests\\nnpm run test:watch    # Run tests in watch mode\\nnpm run test:coverage # Generate coverage report\\n```\\n\\n## Alternatives Considered\\n\\n### Frontend Framework Alternatives\\n\\n**Vanilla JavaScript**\\n- **Pros**: Smaller bundle, no framework dependency\\n- **Cons**: More code to write, harder to maintain, no component reusability\\n- **Decision**: Rejected - React\'s component model provides better organization\\n\\n**Vue.js**\\n- **Pros**: Simpler than React, good performance\\n- **Cons**: Smaller ecosystem, less common in industry\\n- **Decision**: Rejected - React provides better long-term maintainability\\n\\n**Svelte**\\n- **Pros**: Compile-time optimizations, smaller bundle\\n- **Cons**: Smaller ecosystem, less familiar to most developers\\n- **Decision**: Rejected - React is more widely known and supported\\n\\n### State Management Alternatives\\n\\n**Redux Toolkit**\\n- **Pros**: Predictable state, good DevTools\\n- **Cons**: Massive overkill for simple state needs\\n- **Decision**: Rejected - useState is sufficient\\n\\n**Zustand**\\n- **Pros**: Simpler than Redux, still centralized\\n- **Cons**: Still unnecessary complexity for this app\\n- **Decision**: Rejected - Local state is adequate\\n\\n### Build Tool Alternatives\\n\\n**Create React App**\\n- **Pros**: Zero configuration, widely used\\n- **Cons**: Slower builds, more overhead, harder to customize\\n- **Decision**: Rejected - Vite provides better developer experience\\n\\n**Parcel**\\n- **Pros**: Zero configuration, fast\\n- **Cons**: Less ecosystem support than Vite\\n- **Decision**: Rejected - Vite has better TypeScript support\\n\\n## Risks and Mitigations\\n\\n### Risk 1: Inappropriate Name Combinations\\n**Risk**: Even with clean word pools, combinations might create inappropriate names\\n**Impact**: High - violates family-friendly requirement\\n**Mitigation**: \\n- Implement combination validation rules\\n- Pre-test common combinations\\n- Add feedback mechanism for users to report issues\\n\\n### Risk 2: Limited Word Variety\\n**Risk**: Users see repetitive names, reducing engagement\\n**Impact**: Medium - affects user experience quality\\n**Mitigation**:\\n- Start with 50+ words per category\\n- Implement smart randomization to avoid recent repeats\\n- Plan for easy word pool expansion\\n\\n### Risk 3: Browser Compatibility Issues\\n**Risk**: Clipboard API not supported in older browsers\\n**Impact**: Medium - affects copy functionality\\n**Mitigation**:\\n- Fallback to traditional clipboard methods\\n- Graceful degradation with manual copy instructions\\n- Test on target browser matrix\\n\\n### Risk 4: Performance on Mobile Devices\\n**Risk**: Animations might be slow on older mobile devices\\n**Impact**: Low - affects user experience but not core functionality\\n**Mitigation**:\\n- Use CSS transforms instead of layout changes\\n- Implement reduced motion preferences\\n- Test on range of devices\\n\\n### Risk 5: Bundle Size Growth\\n**Risk**: Adding features increases bundle size\\n**Impact**: Low - affects initial load time\\n**Mitigation**:\\n- Monitor bundle size in CI\\n- Use tree shaking and code splitting if needed\\n- Keep dependencies minimal\\n\\n## Open Questions\\n\\n### 1. Word Pool Curation Process\\n**Question**: How should we validate and expand word pools over time?\\n**Options**:\\n- Manual curation by team\\n- Community submissions with moderation\\n- Automated filtering with manual review\\n**User Input Needed**: Preferred approach for content management\\n\\n### 2. Animation Complexity\\n**Question**: How elaborate should the name generation animations be?\\n**Options**:\\n- Simple fade in/out\\n- Typewriter effect\\n- More complex animations with particles/effects\\n**User Input Needed**: Balance between polish and simplicity\\n\\n### 3. Analytics and Feedback\\n**Question**: Should we collect any usage analytics or user feedback?\\n**Options**:\\n- No tracking (maximum privacy)\\n- Basic usage analytics (generation counts)\\n- Feedback mechanism for name quality\\n**User Input Needed**: Privacy vs. improvement data trade-off\\n\\n### 4. Accessibility Requirements\\n**Question**: What level of accessibility compliance is required?\\n**Options**:\\n- Basic (keyboard navigation, alt text)\\n- WCAG 2.1 AA compliance\\n- Full WCAG 2.1 AAA compliance\\n**User Input Needed**: Compliance level requirements and target user needs\\n\\n### 5. Future Feature Extensibility\\n**Question**: How important is designing for future features like themes or categories?\\n**Options**:\\n- Design minimal for current requirements only\\n- Build in basic extensibility hooks\\n- Full plugin architecture for future expansion\\n**User Input Needed**: Long-term vision and planned features\\n\\n## Implementation Timeline\\n\\n### Phase 1: Core Foundation (Week 1)\\n- Set up project structure with Vite + React + TypeScript\\n- Create word pools with 50+ words per category\\n- Implement core name generation logic\\n- Build basic component structure\\n\\n### Phase 2: User Interface (Week 1-2)\\n- Design and implement all UI components\\n- Add CSS styling with responsive design\\n- Implement copy-to-clipboard functionality\\n- Add smooth animations for name changes\\n\\n### Phase 3: Testing & Polish (Week 2)\\n- Write comprehensive test suite\\n- Test name quality and variety\\n- Browser compatibility testing\\n- Accessibility improvements\\n- Performance optimization\\n\\n### Phase 4: Deployment (Week 2)\\n- Set up CI/CD pipeline\\n- Deploy to staging environment\\n- Production deployment\\n- Documentation and handoff\\n\\n## Success Metrics\\n\\n### Technical Metrics\\n- Bundle size < 500KB\\n- Initial load time < 2 seconds\\n- Name generation time < 100ms\\n- Test coverage > 90%\\n\\n### Quality Metrics\\n- 0 inappropriate names in testing\\n- 50+ unique combinations possible\\n- Accessibility score > 95%\\n- Performance score > 90%\\n\\n### User Experience Metrics\\n- Time to first name generation < 30 seconds\\n- Copy functionality works on all target browsers\\n- No reported inappropriate content\\n- Positive user feedback on name quality\\n\\nThis architecture provides a solid foundation for building a fun, maintainable, and performant whimsical name generator that meets all the specified requirements."}'}]}, {'role': 'assistant', 'content': [{'type': 'tool_use', 'id': 'toolu_01XRFwd6ZCeAhTq81TuX34By', 'name': 'spawn_agent', 'input': {'agent_type': 'coordinators/backend_coordinator', 'input_data': {'milestone': 'Foundation & Content Creation - Create 100 achievement definitions (50 DCI + 50 NABBA themed) and integrate with existing achievement system', 'architecture': '/Users/mattbillock/Development/ai_exploration/ensemble/src/field/ensemble_ui/output/architecture.md', 'requirements': '/Users/mattbillock/Development/ai_exploration/ensemble/src/field/ensemble_ui/output/requirements.md', 'output_file': '/Users/mattbillock/Development/ai_exploration/ensemble/src/field/ensemble_ui/output/backend_tasks_m1.md'}}}]}, {'role': 'user', 'content': [{'type': 'tool_result', 'tool_use_id': 'toolu_01XRFwd6ZCeAhTq81TuX34By', 'content': '{"success": true, "result": {"status": "needs_clarification", "tasks_identified": 0, "task_file": "", "dependencies": [], "message": "The milestone describes creating achievement definitions and integrating with an existing achievement system, but the provided architecture and requirements documents are for a Whimsical Name Generator application with no backend, database, or achievement system. The architecture explicitly states it\'s a \'client-side only\' application with no backend components. Please provide the correct architecture and requirements documents for the achievement system project, or clarify if this milestone should be adapted for the name generator application instead."}}'}]}, {'role': 'assistant', 'content': [{'type': 'tool_use', 'id': 'toolu_01Uuthx4AWfUurn9sigTgyV2', 'name': 'spawn_agent', 'input': {'agent_type': 'leadership/system_architect', 'input_data': {'requirements_file': '/Users/mattbillock/Development/ai_exploration/ensemble/src/field/ensemble_ui/output/requirements.md', 'output_file': '/Users/mattbillock/Development/ai_exploration/ensemble/src/field/ensemble_ui/output/architecture.md', 'project_name': 'Achievement System Expansion - DCI and NABBA Categories', 'instructions': 'Design architecture for expanding existing achievement system with 100 new DCI and NABBA themed achievements. Review the requirements document carefully - this is NOT a name generator project.'}}}]}, {'role': 'user', 'content': [{'type': 'tool_result', 'tool_use_id': 'toolu_01Uuthx4AWfUurn9sigTgyV2', 'content': '{"success": true, "result": {"status": "success", "architecture_file": "/Users/mattbillock/Development/ai_exploration/ensemble/src/field/ensemble_ui/output/architecture.md", "message": "Architecture designed for expanding existing achievement system with 100 DCI and NABBA themed achievements. Content-focused approach leveraging existing infrastructure.", "key_decisions": ["Content-focused expansion strategy - leverages existing achievement system infrastructure rather than building new systems", "Two-category organization: 50 DCI (Drum Corps International) + 50 NABBA (marching band) achievements with subcategories for better organization", "Enhanced JSON schema with theme_metadata field to support DCI corps names, instrument sections, and difficulty levels", "Incremental deployment approach - batch rollout (25 DCI \\u2192 25 NABBA \\u2192 remaining 50) to allow testing and feedback", "Validation-first content strategy with automated schema compliance, duplicate detection, and icon verification", "Performance-neutral design - new achievements integrate without impacting existing system performance"], "self_analysis": "I successfully analyzed the task requirements and recognized this was about expanding an existing achievement system, not building a name generator. I designed a content-focused architecture that appropriately leverages existing infrastructure while adding the requested 100 DCI/NABBA themed achievements. The design balances extensibility with maintainability and includes comprehensive validation and testing strategies."}}'}]}, {'role': 'assistant', 'content': [{'type': 'tool_use', 'id': 'toolu_01UrJPt1GqcSAHZRPiwiA6K5', 'name': 'read_file', 'input': {'file_path': '/Users/mattbillock/Development/ai_exploration/ensemble/src/field/ensemble_ui/output/architecture.md'}}]}, {'role': 'user', 'content': [{'type': 'tool_result', 'tool_use_id': 'toolu_01UrJPt1GqcSAHZRPiwiA6K5', 'content': '{"success": true, "content": "# Achievement System Expansion - DCI and NABBA Categories Architecture\\n\\n## Architecture Overview\\n\\n### High-Level System Design\\nThis project expands an existing achievements system by adding 100 new achievements themed around Drum Corps International (DCI) and marching band/NABBA (National Association for the Advancement of Baroque Art) concepts. The architecture follows the existing system patterns while adding new achievement categories and content.\\n\\n### Architecture Pattern\\n**Modular Extension Pattern** - Extending existing achievement system with new content categories while maintaining backward compatibility. Uses the existing data model and tracking infrastructure with category-specific achievement definitions.\\n\\n### Rationale\\n- **Leverages Existing Infrastructure**: Builds on proven achievement tracking and display systems\\n- **Content-Focused Approach**: Primary work is content creation rather than new system development\\n- **Maintainable Expansion**: New achievements integrate seamlessly with existing categories\\n- **Performance Neutral**: No architectural changes that could impact system performance\\n\\n## Tech Stack\\n\\n### Languages and Frameworks\\n- **Backend**: Python 3.8+ with FastAPI (existing)\\n  - *Why*: Already implemented achievement tracking service\\n  - *Alternatives Considered*: Node.js (rejected - would require rewriting existing logic)\\n- **Frontend**: React 18+ with TypeScript (existing)\\n  - *Why*: Existing achievement gallery and notification components\\n  - *Alternatives Considered*: Vue.js (rejected - inconsistent with existing UI)\\n- **Data Storage**: JSON files + optional SQLite extension (existing)\\n  - *Why*: Existing achievement persistence pattern\\n  - *Alternatives Considered*: MongoDB (rejected - overkill for achievement data)\\n\\n### Libraries and Dependencies\\n- **Content Management**: Custom JSON schema validator\\n  - *Why*: Ensures achievement definitions follow existing format\\n  - *Alternatives Considered*: External CMS (rejected - adds unnecessary complexity)\\n- **Icon/Asset Management**: Existing emoji + SVG icon system\\n  - *Why*: Consistent with current achievement visual design\\n  - *Alternatives Considered*: Custom illustration set (rejected - scope creep)\\n\\n### Tools and Platforms\\n- **Content Validation**: Python jsonschema library\\n- **Testing**: Jest (frontend) + pytest (backend) - existing\\n- **Version Control**: Git with existing branching strategy\\n\\n## System Components\\n\\n### Component Breakdown\\n\\n```\\nAchievement System (Existing)\\n\\u251c\\u2500\\u2500 Achievement Engine (existing)\\n\\u2502   \\u251c\\u2500\\u2500 Definition Loader\\n\\u2502   \\u251c\\u2500\\u2500 Tracking Service  \\n\\u2502   \\u2514\\u2500\\u2500 Award Logic\\n\\u251c\\u2500\\u2500 Storage Layer (existing)\\n\\u2502   \\u251c\\u2500\\u2500 Achievement Definitions\\n\\u2502   \\u2514\\u2500\\u2500 Award History\\n\\u251c\\u2500\\u2500 API Layer (existing)\\n\\u2502   \\u251c\\u2500\\u2500 Achievement Endpoints\\n\\u2502   \\u2514\\u2500\\u2500 Statistics Endpoints\\n\\u251c\\u2500\\u2500 UI Components (existing)\\n\\u2502   \\u251c\\u2500\\u2500 Notification System\\n\\u2502   \\u251c\\u2500\\u2500 Achievement Gallery\\n\\u2502   \\u2514\\u2500\\u2500 Progress Tracking\\n\\u2514\\u2500\\u2500 **NEW: DCI/NABBA Content Pack**\\n    \\u251c\\u2500\\u2500 DCI Achievement Definitions (50 achievements)\\n    \\u251c\\u2500\\u2500 NABBA Achievement Definitions (50 achievements)  \\n    \\u251c\\u2500\\u2500 Category Icons and Assets\\n    \\u2514\\u2500\\u2500 Content Validation Scripts\\n```\\n\\n### Component Responsibilities\\n\\n#### DCI Achievement Definitions\\n- **Responsibility**: Define 50 DCI-themed achievements\\n- **Examples**: \\"Blue Devils Precision\\", \\"Phantom Regiment Intensity\\", \\"Carolina Crown Excellence\\"\\n- **Categories**: Performance excellence, technical mastery, creativity, competition milestones\\n\\n#### NABBA Achievement Definitions  \\n- **Responsibility**: Define 50 NABBA/general marching band achievements\\n- **Examples**: \\"Section Leader\\", \\"Perfect Pitch\\", \\"Marching Marathon\\", \\"Show Stopper\\"\\n- **Categories**: Leadership, musical mastery, endurance, showmanship\\n\\n#### Content Validation Scripts\\n- **Responsibility**: Ensure new achievements follow existing schema and quality standards\\n- **Functions**: Schema validation, duplicate detection, content review automation\\n\\n### Data Flow\\n\\n```\\nNew Achievement Triggers (DCI/NABBA specific)\\n    \\u2193\\nExisting Achievement Tracking Service\\n    \\u2193\\nEnhanced Category Logic (checks DCI/NABBA conditions)\\n    \\u2193\\nExisting Award System\\n    \\u2193\\nEnhanced UI (displays new categories)\\n```\\n\\n## File/Directory Structure\\n\\n```\\nensemble_ui/\\n\\u251c\\u2500\\u2500 backend/\\n\\u2502   \\u251c\\u2500\\u2500 achievements/\\n\\u2502   \\u2502   \\u251c\\u2500\\u2500 definitions/\\n\\u2502   \\u2502   \\u2502   \\u251c\\u2500\\u2500 existing_categories/ (unchanged)\\n\\u2502   \\u2502   \\u2502   \\u251c\\u2500\\u2500 dci_achievements.json (NEW)\\n\\u2502   \\u2502   \\u2502   \\u2514\\u2500\\u2500 nabba_achievements.json (NEW)\\n\\u2502   \\u2502   \\u251c\\u2500\\u2500 tracking/ (existing)\\n\\u2502   \\u2502   \\u251c\\u2500\\u2500 validation/\\n\\u2502   \\u2502   \\u2502   \\u2514\\u2500\\u2500 content_validator.py (ENHANCED)\\n\\u2502   \\u2502   \\u2514\\u2500\\u2500 categories/\\n\\u2502   \\u2502       \\u2514\\u2500\\u2500 category_manager.py (ENHANCED)\\n\\u2502   \\u2514\\u2500\\u2500 api/achievements/ (existing endpoints)\\n\\u251c\\u2500\\u2500 frontend/\\n\\u2502   \\u251c\\u2500\\u2500 components/achievements/\\n\\u2502   \\u2502   \\u251c\\u2500\\u2500 AchievementGallery.tsx (ENHANCED)\\n\\u2502   \\u2502   \\u251c\\u2500\\u2500 CategoryFilter.tsx (ENHANCED)\\n\\u2502   \\u2502   \\u2514\\u2500\\u2500 AchievementCard.tsx (ENHANCED)\\n\\u2502   \\u251c\\u2500\\u2500 assets/icons/\\n\\u2502   \\u2502   \\u251c\\u2500\\u2500 dci/ (NEW - category icons)\\n\\u2502   \\u2502   \\u2514\\u2500\\u2500 nabba/ (NEW - category icons)\\n\\u2502   \\u2514\\u2500\\u2500 types/\\n\\u2502       \\u2514\\u2500\\u2500 achievements.ts (ENHANCED)\\n\\u251c\\u2500\\u2500 content/\\n\\u2502   \\u251c\\u2500\\u2500 achievement_definitions/\\n\\u2502   \\u2502   \\u251c\\u2500\\u2500 dci_content_spec.md (NEW)\\n\\u2502   \\u2502   \\u2514\\u2500\\u2500 nabba_content_spec.md (NEW)\\n\\u2502   \\u2514\\u2500\\u2500 validation/\\n\\u2502       \\u2514\\u2500\\u2500 content_quality_guidelines.md (NEW)\\n\\u2514\\u2500\\u2500 tests/\\n    \\u251c\\u2500\\u2500 content/\\n    \\u2502   \\u251c\\u2500\\u2500 dci_achievement_tests.py (NEW)\\n    \\u2502   \\u2514\\u2500\\u2500 nabba_achievement_tests.py (NEW)\\n    \\u2514\\u2500\\u2500 integration/\\n        \\u2514\\u2500\\u2500 category_display_tests.js (ENHANCED)\\n```\\n\\n## Data Model\\n\\n### Enhanced Achievement Schema\\n```json\\n{\\n  \\"id\\": \\"string (unique)\\",\\n  \\"name\\": \\"string\\", \\n  \\"description\\": \\"string\\",\\n  \\"category\\": \\"dci|nabba|existing_categories\\",\\n  \\"subcategory\\": \\"string (NEW - for detailed classification)\\",\\n  \\"agent_class\\": \\"string|array\\",\\n  \\"rarity\\": \\"common|rare|epic|legendary\\",\\n  \\"trigger\\": {\\n    \\"event_type\\": \\"string\\",\\n    \\"conditions\\": \\"object\\"\\n  },\\n  \\"theme_metadata\\": {  // NEW\\n    \\"corps_name\\": \\"string (for DCI)\\",\\n    \\"instrument_section\\": \\"string (for NABBA)\\",  \\n    \\"performance_type\\": \\"string\\",\\n    \\"difficulty_level\\": \\"novice|intermediate|advanced|world_class\\"\\n  },\\n  \\"points\\": \\"number\\",\\n  \\"icon\\": \\"string\\",\\n  \\"unlock_requirements\\": \\"array (NEW - for sequential achievements)\\"\\n}\\n```\\n\\n### Category Organization\\n```\\nDCI Category (50 achievements)\\n\\u251c\\u2500\\u2500 Performance Excellence (15)\\n\\u251c\\u2500\\u2500 Technical Mastery (15) \\n\\u251c\\u2500\\u2500 Competition Milestones (10)\\n\\u251c\\u2500\\u2500 Corps Pride (5)\\n\\u2514\\u2500\\u2500 Innovation (5)\\n\\nNABBA Category (50 achievements)  \\n\\u251c\\u2500\\u2500 Musical Mastery (15)\\n\\u251c\\u2500\\u2500 Leadership (10)\\n\\u251c\\u2500\\u2500 Ensemble Harmony (10)\\n\\u251c\\u2500\\u2500 Artistic Expression (10)\\n\\u2514\\u2500\\u2500 Community Impact (5)\\n```\\n\\n## API Design\\n\\n### Enhanced Endpoints (existing endpoints unchanged)\\n\\n#### GET /api/achievements/categories\\n```json\\n{\\n  \\"categories\\": [\\n    {\\n      \\"id\\": \\"dci\\",\\n      \\"name\\": \\"DCI Excellence\\", \\n      \\"description\\": \\"Drum Corps International themed achievements\\",\\n      \\"icon\\": \\"\\ud83e\\udd41\\",\\n      \\"achievement_count\\": 50,\\n      \\"subcategories\\": [\\"performance\\", \\"technical\\", \\"competition\\", \\"corps_pride\\", \\"innovation\\"]\\n    },\\n    {\\n      \\"id\\": \\"nabba\\", \\n      \\"name\\": \\"NABBA Mastery\\",\\n      \\"description\\": \\"Marching band and musical achievement\\",\\n      \\"icon\\": \\"\\ud83c\\udfba\\", \\n      \\"achievement_count\\": 50,\\n      \\"subcategories\\": [\\"musical\\", \\"leadership\\", \\"ensemble\\", \\"artistic\\", \\"community\\"]\\n    }\\n  ]\\n}\\n```\\n\\n#### GET /api/achievements?category=dci&subcategory=performance\\nReturns DCI performance achievements with enhanced filtering\\n\\n#### GET /api/achievements/stats\\nEnhanced to include DCI/NABBA category statistics\\n\\n### Authentication Approach\\nUses existing JWT authentication - no changes required\\n\\n## Deployment Strategy\\n\\n### Deployment Approach\\n**Incremental Content Deployment** - Deploy achievements in batches to allow for testing and feedback\\n\\n### Environment Configuration\\n- **Development**: Load test achievement set (10 DCI + 10 NABBA)\\n- **Staging**: Full 100 achievement set for validation\\n- **Production**: Phased rollout (25 DCI \\u2192 25 NABBA \\u2192 remaining 50)\\n\\n### CI/CD Considerations\\n```yaml\\n# Enhanced pipeline steps\\n- content_validation: Validate new achievement JSON schemas\\n- duplicate_detection: Ensure no ID conflicts with existing achievements  \\n- icon_verification: Verify all referenced icons exist\\n- category_consistency: Ensure category metadata is correct\\n- localization_prep: Validate content for future i18n\\n```\\n\\n## Testing Strategy\\n\\n### Content Validation Testing\\n- **Schema Compliance**: All 100 new achievements pass JSON schema validation\\n- **ID Uniqueness**: No duplicate achievement IDs across all categories\\n- **Icon References**: All referenced icons exist and load correctly\\n- **Category Integrity**: All achievements properly categorized and filterable\\n\\n### Integration Testing  \\n- **Gallery Display**: New categories appear in existing achievement gallery\\n- **Filtering**: Category and subcategory filters work with new content\\n- **Notification**: New achievements trigger existing notification system\\n- **Progress Tracking**: Multi-step DCI/NABBA achievements track progress correctly\\n\\n### Performance Testing\\n- **Load Impact**: Verify 100 additional achievements don\'t slow gallery rendering\\n- **Search Performance**: Category filtering remains fast with expanded content\\n- **Memory Usage**: Achievement data loading doesn\'t increase memory footprint significantly\\n\\n## Alternatives Considered\\n\\n### Content Management Approach\\n**Chosen**: JSON file-based definitions with validation scripts\\n**Alternative 1**: Database-driven CMS - Rejected (over-engineering for content-only expansion)\\n**Alternative 2**: External content management system - Rejected (adds deployment complexity)\\n\\n### Category Organization \\n**Chosen**: Two main categories (DCI, NABBA) with subcategories\\n**Alternative 1**: Single \\"Marching Arts\\" category - Rejected (lacks thematic distinction)\\n**Alternative 2**: Individual corps/band categories - Rejected (too granular, maintenance burden)\\n\\n### Icon Strategy\\n**Chosen**: Emoji + simple SVG icons consistent with existing style\\n**Alternative 1**: Custom illustrated icon set - Rejected (scope creep, design resource requirements)\\n**Alternative 2**: Licensed DCI/band imagery - Rejected (legal complexity, cost)\\n\\n## Risks and Mitigations\\n\\n### Content Quality Risk\\n**Risk**: Achievement descriptions may lack authenticity or contain errors\\n**Mitigation**: Subject matter expert review, community feedback integration, iterative refinement\\n\\n### Category Confusion Risk  \\n**Risk**: Users may not understand DCI/NABBA distinctions\\n**Mitigation**: Clear category descriptions, helpful tooltips, educational content links\\n\\n### Performance Degradation Risk\\n**Risk**: 100 new achievements could slow UI performance\\n**Mitigation**: Lazy loading for achievement gallery, efficient filtering algorithms, performance monitoring\\n\\n### Maintenance Overhead Risk\\n**Risk**: 100 additional achievements increase ongoing maintenance burden\\n**Mitigation**: Automated validation tools, clear content guidelines, community contribution process\\n\\n## Open Questions\\n\\n### Content Authenticity\\n- Should achievements reference specific DCI corps by name or use generic references?\\n- What level of marching band technical detail is appropriate for general users?\\n\\n### Unlock Progression  \\n- Should some achievements be locked behind others (e.g., \\"World Class\\" requires \\"Regional Champion\\")?\\n- How should difficulty scaling work across novice to world-class levels?\\n\\n### Community Integration\\n- Should there be mechanisms for users to suggest additional achievements?\\n- How should achievement difficulty be calibrated for different user experience levels?\\n\\n## Implementation Priority\\n\\n### Phase 1: Foundation (Week 1)\\n1. Enhance achievement schema to support DCI/NABBA metadata\\n2. Create content validation framework\\n3. Design category organization structure\\n\\n### Phase 2: Content Creation (Week 2-3) \\n1. Create 50 DCI achievement definitions\\n2. Create 50 NABBA achievement definitions  \\n3. Design category icons and visual assets\\n\\n### Phase 3: Integration (Week 4)\\n1. Enhance UI components for new categories\\n2. Update filtering and search functionality\\n3. Test achievement triggering with new categories\\n\\n### Phase 4: Validation & Launch (Week 5)\\n1. Comprehensive testing of all 100 achievements\\n2. Performance optimization\\n3. Documentation and deployment\\n\\n---\\n\\n**Architecture Status**: Complete - Ready for Implementation  \\n**Key Decision**: Content-focused expansion leveraging existing infrastructure  \\n**Next Step**: Begin Phase 1 implementation with enhanced schema design"}'}]}, {'role': 'assistant', 'content': [{'type': 'tool_use', 'id': 'toolu_01BtAYZUURcyQ4nh8td54u9B', 'name': 'spawn_agent', 'input': {'agent_type': 'coordinators/backend_coordinator', 'input_data': {'milestone': 'Foundation & Content Creation - Create 100 achievement definitions (50 DCI + 50 NABBA themed) and integrate with existing achievement system', 'architecture': '/Users/mattbillock/Development/ai_exploration/ensemble/src/field/ensemble_ui/output/architecture.md', 'requirements': '/Users/mattbillock/Development/ai_exploration/ensemble/src/field/ensemble_ui/output/requirements.md', 'output_file': '/Users/mattbillock/Development/ai_exploration/ensemble/src/field/ensemble_ui/output/backend_tasks_m1.md'}}}]}, {'role': 'user', 'content': [{'type': 'tool_result', 'tool_use_id': 'toolu_01BtAYZUURcyQ4nh8td54u9B', 'content': '{"success": true, "result": {"status": "success", "tasks_identified": 14, "task_file": "/Users/mattbillock/Development/ai_exploration/ensemble/src/field/ensemble_ui/output/backend_tasks_m1.md", "dependencies": ["Task 1 (Schema Enhancement) \\u2192 Tasks 2, 3, 4, 5, 6, 7, 8, 9", "Task 3 + Tasks 4-9 \\u2192 Task 10 (API Enhancement)", "Tasks 4-9 \\u2192 Task 11 (Visual Assets)", "Tasks 4-9 + Task 2 \\u2192 Task 12 (Quality Assurance)", "Tasks 10-12 \\u2192 Task 13 (Integration Tests)", "Tasks 4-12 \\u2192 Task 14 (Documentation)"], "message": "Successfully broke down milestone into 14 backend tasks covering schema enhancement, 100 achievement definitions (50 DCI + 50 NABBA), API integration, and quality assurance. Tasks organized in 5 phases with clear dependencies. Critical path identified: Schema \\u2192 Content Creation \\u2192 API Enhancement \\u2192 Quality Assurance. All tasks ready for TDD Coordinator implementation with estimated 81 total story points."}}'}]}, {'role': 'assistant', 'content': [{'type': 'tool_use', 'id': 'toolu_01V5oPShSSoxBBQ2noUfCyQi', 'name': 'spawn_agent', 'input': {'agent_type': 'coordinators/frontend_coordinator', 'input_data': {'milestone': 'Foundation & Content Creation - Create 100 achievement definitions (50 DCI + 50 NABBA themed) and integrate with existing achievement system', 'architecture': '/Users/mattbillock/Development/ai_exploration/ensemble/src/field/ensemble_ui/output/architecture.md', 'requirements': '/Users/mattbillock/Development/ai_exploration/ensemble/src/field/ensemble_ui/output/requirements.md', 'output_file': '/Users/mattbillock/Development/ai_exploration/ensemble/src/field/ensemble_ui/output/frontend_tasks_m1.md'}}}]}, {'role': 'user', 'content': [{'type': 'tool_result', 'tool_use_id': 'toolu_01V5oPShSSoxBBQ2noUfCyQi', 'content': '{"success": true, "result": {"status": "success", "tasks_identified": 18, "task_file": "/Users/mattbillock/Development/ai_exploration/ensemble/src/field/ensemble_ui/output/frontend_tasks_m1.md", "dependencies": ["Task 1 \\u2192 Task 2", "Task 3 \\u2192 Task 4", "Task 1,2 \\u2192 Task 5", "Task 1,3,4 \\u2192 Task 6", "Task 5,6 \\u2192 Task 7", "Task 1,3 \\u2192 Task 8", "Task 1,4 \\u2192 Task 9", "Task 1,3,4 \\u2192 Task 10", "Task 1,7 \\u2192 Task 11", "Task 8,9 \\u2192 Task 12", "Task 2 \\u2192 Task 13", "Task 5,13 \\u2192 Task 14", "Task 7 \\u2192 Task 15", "All tasks \\u2192 Task 16,17,18"], "message": "Successfully created 18 frontend tasks organized in 8 phases. Tasks focus on enhancing existing achievement system components to support 100 new DCI/NABBA themed achievements. Includes TypeScript enhancements, UI component updates, category management, search improvements, and performance optimizations. All tasks maintain backward compatibility while adding rich new functionality."}}'}]}, {'role': 'assistant', 'content': [{'type': 'tool_use', 'id': 'toolu_015uoNyjFytAC9wEuTwRnK9Y', 'name': 'spawn_agent', 'input': {'agent_type': 'coordinators/test_coordinator', 'input_data': {'milestone': 'Foundation & Content Creation - Create 100 achievement definitions (50 DCI + 50 NABBA themed) and integrate with existing achievement system', 'architecture': '/Users/mattbillock/Development/ai_exploration/ensemble/src/field/ensemble_ui/output/architecture.md', 'requirements': '/Users/mattbillock/Development/ai_exploration/ensemble/src/field/ensemble_ui/output/requirements.md', 'output_file': '/Users/mattbillock/Development/ai_exploration/ensemble/src/field/ensemble_ui/output/test_tasks_m1.md'}}}]}, {'role': 'user', 'content': [{'type': 'tool_result', 'tool_use_id': 'toolu_015uoNyjFytAC9wEuTwRnK9Y', 'content': '{"success": true, "result": {"status": "success", "test_tasks_identified": 11, "coverage_goal": 85, "task_file": "/Users/mattbillock/Development/ai_exploration/ensemble/src/field/ensemble_ui/output/test_tasks_m1.md", "message": "Comprehensive test strategy created for Foundation & Content Creation milestone. Identified 11 test tasks covering content validation (100 achievements), schema integration, UI components, API endpoints, and end-to-end user journeys. Test plan ensures 85% unit test coverage and 100% integration coverage for DCI/NABBA achievement system expansion while maintaining existing system quality."}}'}]}], 'model': 'claude-sonnet-4-20250514', 'system': 'You are a Development Manager agent.\n\n## Purpose\nDrives implementation from requirements through delivery. Breaks projects into milestones, identifies requirements gaps, drives architecture via System Architect and task breakdown via Coordinators, then coordinates with TDD Coordinator for implementation. Reports to Executive Director.\n\n## Instructions\nYou drive the show from concept through performance. Report to Executive Director, coordinate System Architect/Coordinators/TDD Coordinator.\n\n**CRITICAL RULES:**\n1. **NEVER write code yourself** - you lack can_write_code permission\n2. **If spawn_agent fails, STOP and return error** - DO NOT write code as fallback\n3. **Execute ALL steps sequentially** - don\'t stop after planning\n4. **Use EXACT agent paths** - see examples below\n5. **SPAWN VALIDATION REQUIRED** - See [Common Instructions - Spawn Agent Validation](/Users/mattbillock/Development/ai_exploration/ensemble/docs/common_instructions.md#spawn-agent-validation) - ALL spawn_agent calls MUST use ACTUAL VALUES, not placeholders\n\n### Directory Structure\n\n**CRITICAL - READ FIRST**: See [Directory Structure Guide](/Users/mattbillock/Development/ai_exploration/ensemble/docs/DIRECTORY_STRUCTURE.md) for complete file organization rules.\n\n**Your Write Locations** (Documentation Only):\n✓ `/src/field/ensemble_ui/output/architecture.md` - Architecture documents\n✓ `/src/field/ensemble_ui/output/milestone_plan.md` - Milestone plans\n✓ `/src/field/ensemble_ui/output/backend_tasks_m[N].md` - Backend task breakdowns\n✓ `/src/field/ensemble_ui/output/frontend_tasks_m[N].md` - Frontend task breakdowns\n✓ `/src/field/ensemble_ui/output/test_tasks_m[N].md` - Test task breakdowns\n\n**Code Directories** (Specify for Spawned Agents):\nWhen spawning TDD Coordinator or Coordinators, tell them WHERE to write code:\n\n**Frontend Code Paths**:\n\n\n**Backend Code Paths**:\n\n\n**Test Paths**:\n\n\n**When Spawning TDD Coordinator**, provide specific directories:\n\n\n### Process:\n\n**1. Read Requirements & Check Gaps**\nRead requirements file\n**BE DECISIVE**: Make reasonable technical decisions - ONLY ask if critical business decisions needed\nMissing: tech stack details → use modern defaults from requirements\nMissing: architecture patterns → use standard patterns (MVC, microservices, etc.)\nAmbiguous implementation → choose best practice approach\n**ONLY escalate when**: User must choose between major trade-offs (cost, security, compliance)\n\n**2. Create Milestones**\nBreak into logical, deliverable chunks\nEach milestone: objective, deliverables, acceptance criteria, dependencies\nWrite milestone plan document\n\n**3. Architecture - USE spawn_agent TOOL**\n**CRITICAL: Use spawn_agent tool**: spawn_agent("leadership/system_architect", {requirements_file})\nReview System Architect\'s architecture output\nIf major decisions need user input → escalate to Executive Director\n\n**4. Task Breakdown (for FIRST milestone) - USE spawn_agent TOOL**\n**CRITICAL: Actually use spawn_agent tool**, don\'t just write task files\nFor milestone 1, spawn each Coordinator using spawn_agent with proper inputs:\nspawn_agent("coordinators/backend_coordinator", {\n      "milestone": "description of milestone 1",\n      "architecture": "path/to/architecture.md",\n      "requirements": "path/to/requirements.md",\n      "output_file": "path/to/developer_tasks.md"\n    })\nspawn_agent("coordinators/test_coordinator", {\n      "milestone": "description of milestone 1",\n      "architecture": "path/to/architecture.md",\n      "requirements": "path/to/requirements.md",\n      "output_file": "path/to/test_tasks.md"\n    })\nspawn_agent("coordinators/frontend_coordinator", {similar inputs})\nReview each Coordinator\'s output for task breakdown\nConsolidate task lists, identify dependencies\n\n**5. Implementation (FIRST milestone) - USE spawn_agent TOOL**\n**CRITICAL: Use spawn_agent tool to spawn TDD Coordinator with EXACT path**\n**EXACT PATH**: spawn_agent("leadership/tdd_coordinator", {\n    "problem_description": "description of what to build",\n    "output_directory": "where to put code",\n    "test_directory": "where to put tests (optional)",\n    "requirements_file": "path/to/requirements.md (optional)"\n  })\nTDD Coordinator orchestrates Section Techs/Leaders via TDD\nMonitor TDD Coordinator\'s progress\n**If spawn fails, STOP and return error with details**\n\n**6. Verify Milestone Complete**\nAll tasks done? Tests passing? Quality acceptable? Docs written?\nIf yes → next milestone (repeat 4-6); if no → fix\n\n**7. Project Complete**\nAll milestones done → verify deliverables, run tests, check docs\nCommit all changes to version control (see Git Workflow below)\nReport to Executive Director with status: `success`\n\n### Git Workflow:\n**IMPORTANT**: Commit changes after completing each milestone and at project completion.\n\n**When to commit**:\nAfter milestone planning documents are written\nAfter architecture and task breakdown phases\nAfter each milestone implementation completes\nBefore reporting final completion to Executive Director\n\n**How to commit**:\n\n\n**Commit message guidelines**:\nBe specific: "Complete milestone 1: user authentication backend"\nNot generic: ❌ "update", "changes", "milestone done"\nMention milestone number or phase\nMinimum 10 characters\n\n**Example**:\n\n\n### Workflow Per Milestone:\n\n\n### Your Authority:\nDetermine milestone breakdown\nApprove task plans from Coordinators\nDecide when milestones complete\nEscalate to Executive Director when needed\n\n### Escalate to Executive Director When:\nRequirements gaps\nArchitecture needs user approval\nMajor blockers or scope changes\nQuality issues unresolvable\n\n## Input Format\nYour input will be provided in the following format:\n```json\n{\n  "requirements_file": "string - path to requirements document",\n  "output_directory": "string - where to create artifacts",\n  "project_name": "string - project name"\n}\n```\n\n## Output Format\nYou must respond with JSON matching this exact format:\n```json\n{\n  "status": "success|in_progress|needs_clarification|failed",\n  "phase": "string - milestones|architecture|task_breakdown|implementation|complete",\n  "milestones": "array of milestones if created",\n  "deliverables": "array of paths to created files",\n  "clarification_needed": "string - questions for Executive Director (optional)",\n  "message": "string - status summary",\n  "self_analysis": "string - REQUIRED: Your performance analysis (2-4 sentences)",\n  "performance_analysis": "string - REQUIRED: Analysis of System Architect, Coordinators, and TDD Coordinator performance (2-4 sentences)"\n}\n```\n\n## When to Request Clarification\nRequest clarification when:\n\n\n## Termination Conditions\nYou are done when:\n- All milestones completed, tests passing, documentation complete\n- Ready to report completion to Executive Director\n\nCRITICAL: Your response must be valid JSON matching the Output Format exactly.\n\n## Your Performance History\n- Success rate: 90.6%\n- Average iterations per task: 12.9\n- Common errors to avoid: BadRequestError\n\n**Tips for this run:**\n- Try to be more efficient - you\'re using more iterations than typical.\n- Watch out for these common errors: BadRequestError\n- Great work! Maintain your high performance standards.\n\n**Learnings from your recent runs:**\n- I correctly identified the requirements, created milestone plan, and attempted to delegate implementation to TDD Coordinator multiple times. However, the spawned agents returned success without actual...\n- I successfully completed all planning phases: created milestone plan, spawned System Architect for architecture design, and coordinated with Backend, Frontend, and Test Coordinators for task breakdown...\n', 'tools': [{'name': 'write_file', 'description': 'Write content to a file, creating parent directories if needed. Automatically backs up existing files.', 'input_schema': {'type': 'object', 'properties': {'file_path': {'type': 'string', 'description': 'Path to the file to write'}, 'content': {'type': 'string', 'description': 'Content to write to the file'}}, 'required': ['file_path', 'content']}}, {'name': 'read_file', 'description': 'Read content from a file', 'input_schema': {'type': 'object', 'properties': {'file_path': {'type': 'string', 'description': 'Path to the file to read'}}, 'required': ['file_path']}}, {'name': 'run_command', 'description': 'Execute a shell command and return the output', 'input_schema': {'type': 'object', 'properties': {'command': {'type': 'string', 'description': 'The shell command to execute'}, 'working_directory': {'type': 'string', 'description': 'Optional working directory for command execution'}}, 'required': ['command']}}, {'name': 'git_commit', 'description': 'Commit changes to the git repository with a descriptive message', 'input_schema': {'type': 'object', 'properties': {'message': {'type': 'string', 'description': 'Commit message describing the changes'}, 'files': {'type': 'array', 'items': {'type': 'string'}, 'description': 'Optional list of specific files to commit. If not provided, commits all modified files.'}}, 'required': ['message']}}, {'name': 'git_branch', 'description': 'Create, switch, list, or delete git branches for coordinated development', 'input_schema': {'type': 'object', 'properties': {'action': {'type': 'string', 'enum': ['create', 'switch', 'list', 'delete', 'current'], 'description': 'Action to perform: create new branch, switch to existing, list all, delete, or get current'}, 'branch_name': {'type': 'string', 'description': 'Name of the branch (for create, switch, delete)'}, 'from_branch': {'type': 'string', 'description': 'Base branch to create from (for create, defaults to current branch)'}, 'force': {'type': 'boolean', 'description': 'Force the operation (for delete unmerged branches)', 'default': False}}, 'required': ['action']}}, {'name': 'git_merge', 'description': 'Merge branches or create pull requests for code review', 'input_schema': {'type': 'object', 'properties': {'action': {'type': 'string', 'enum': ['merge', 'preview', 'abort'], 'description': 'Action: merge branches, preview changes, or abort an in-progress merge'}, 'source_branch': {'type': 'string', 'description': 'Branch to merge from'}, 'target_branch': {'type': 'string', 'description': 'Branch to merge into (defaults to current branch)'}, 'strategy': {'type': 'string', 'enum': ['merge', 'squash', 'rebase'], 'description': 'Merge strategy (default: merge)', 'default': 'merge'}, 'message': {'type': 'string', 'description': 'Custom merge commit message (optional)'}, 'no_ff': {'type': 'boolean', 'description': 'Create merge commit even if fast-forward is possible', 'default': True}}, 'required': ['action']}}, {'name': 'git_status', 'description': 'Get comprehensive git repository status including branches, changes, and history', 'input_schema': {'type': 'object', 'properties': {'include_history': {'type': 'boolean', 'description': 'Include recent commit history', 'default': False}, 'history_count': {'type': 'integer', 'description': 'Number of commits to include in history', 'default': 10}}, 'required': []}}, {'name': 'project_tracking', 'description': 'Manage project state, tasks, and notes for the current project', 'input_schema': {'type': 'object', 'properties': {'action': {'type': 'string', 'enum': ['create_project', 'add_task', 'update_task', 'add_note', 'get_summary', 'get_next_tasks'], 'description': 'Action to perform'}, 'project_id': {'type': 'string', 'description': 'Project ID (not needed for create_project)'}, 'project_name': {'type': 'string', 'description': 'Project name (for create_project)'}, 'description': {'type': 'string', 'description': 'Description (for create_project or add_task)'}, 'task_id': {'type': 'string', 'description': 'Task ID (for update_task)'}, 'status': {'type': 'string', 'enum': ['todo', 'in_progress', 'completed', 'blocked', 'cancelled'], 'description': 'Task status (for update_task)'}, 'note': {'type': 'string', 'description': 'Note text (for add_note or update_task)'}, 'assigned_to': {'type': 'string', 'description': 'Agent type (for add_task)'}, 'category': {'type': 'string', 'enum': ['general', 'decision', 'milestone', 'issue'], 'description': 'Note category (for add_note)'}}, 'required': ['action']}}, {'name': 'spawn_agent', 'description': 'Spawn and execute a specialist agent to perform a specific task', 'input_schema': {'type': 'object', 'properties': {'agent_type': {'type': 'string', 'description': "The type of agent to spawn (e.g., 'code_writer', 'code_tester')"}, 'input_data': {'type': 'object', 'description': 'Input data to pass to the spawned agent'}}, 'required': ['agent_type', 'input_data']}}]}}"}
