{"timestamp": "2026-01-14 21:04:10", "level": "DEBUG", "module": "anthropic._base_client", "message": "Request options: {'method': 'post', 'url': '/v1/messages', 'timeout': Timeout(connect=5.0, read=600, write=600, pool=600), 'files': None, 'idempotency_key': 'stainless-python-retry-9f49e868-65e3-4d86-b2f2-614f5a324867', 'json_data': {'max_tokens': 4096, 'messages': [{'role': 'user', 'content': 'Please complete the following task:\n\n{\n  "problem_description": "Expand existing achievement system with 100 new achievements (50 DCI-themed + 50 NABBA-themed) while maintaining full integration with existing tracking, display, and API systems. Create achievement definitions with cultural authenticity, enhance schema to support theme metadata, update UI for category filtering, and ensure performance remains optimal.",\n  "output_directory": "/Users/mattbillock/Development/ai_exploration/ensemble/src/field/ensemble_ui",\n  "requirements_file": "/Users/mattbillock/Development/ai_exploration/ensemble/src/field/ensemble_ui/output/requirements.md"\n}\n\nRemember to respond with valid JSON matching the expected output format.\n'}, {'role': 'assistant', 'content': [{'type': 'tool_use', 'id': 'toolu_01EcYSYeNTtU22m28MnNPWc3', 'name': 'read_file', 'input': {'file_path': '/Users/mattbillock/Development/ai_exploration/ensemble/src/field/ensemble_ui/output/requirements.md'}}]}, {'role': 'user', 'content': [{'type': 'tool_result', 'tool_use_id': 'toolu_01EcYSYeNTtU22m28MnNPWc3', 'content': '{"success": true, "content": "# Whimsical Name Generator - Requirements\\n\\n## Project Overview\\n\\n### Vision\\nCreate a fun, family-friendly whimsical name generator that produces unique, creative names to replace boring default names like \\"exec_dir_1\\". The generator should create names with personality and charm, such as \\"Whimsy Cloud Strider\\" or \\"Edge Citrusy Edge\\".\\n\\n### Core Problem\\nUsers are tired of boring, generic default names and want something fun and memorable that adds personality to their experience.\\n\\n### Solution\\nA whimsical name generator that combines creative adjectives, nouns, and descriptors to create unique, family-friendly names on demand.\\n\\n## Functional Requirements\\n\\n### Core Features\\n1. **Random Name Generation**\\n   - Generate unique whimsical names on demand\\n   - Combine multiple word categories (adjectives, nouns, descriptors)\\n   - Ensure family-friendly content only\\n\\n2. **Name Components**\\n   - Whimsical adjectives (Whimsy, Citrusy, Sparkly, Dreamy, etc.)\\n   - Nature/fantasy nouns (Cloud, Edge, Storm, Meadow, etc.)  \\n   - Action/descriptor words (Strider, Walker, Keeper, Singer, etc.)\\n\\n3. **User Interface**\\n   - Simple button to generate new name\\n   - Display current generated name prominently\\n   - Option to regenerate if user doesn\'t like current name\\n   - Copy-to-clipboard functionality\\n\\n4. **Name Quality**\\n   - All names must be family-friendly\\n   - Names should be memorable and fun\\n   - Avoid repetitive or boring combinations\\n   - 2-3 word combinations for good flow\\n\\n### Technical Requirements\\n1. **Frontend (React)**\\n   - Responsive design that works on all devices\\n   - Clean, playful UI design\\n   - Smooth animations for name generation\\n   - Accessible controls and text\\n\\n2. **Name Generation Logic**\\n   - Client-side generation for instant response\\n   - Large word pools to ensure variety\\n   - Smart combination logic to avoid awkward phrings\\n   - Randomization that feels truly random to users\\n\\n## Non-Functional Requirements\\n\\n### Performance\\n- Instant name generation (< 100ms)\\n- Lightweight implementation\\n- No external API dependencies needed\\n\\n### Usability\\n- One-click name generation\\n- Clear, readable typography\\n- Intuitive interface requiring no instructions\\n\\n### Content Standards\\n- All generated names must be appropriate for all ages\\n- No offensive, scary, or inappropriate word combinations\\n- Positive, uplifting tone in all generated content\\n\\n## User Stories\\n\\n1. **As a user**, I want to click a button and instantly get a fun, whimsical name so I can replace boring default names.\\n\\n2. **As a user**, I want to regenerate names until I find one I like so I can get the perfect name for my needs.\\n\\n3. **As a user**, I want to easily copy the generated name so I can use it elsewhere.\\n\\n4. **As a parent**, I want all generated names to be family-friendly so I can safely use this with my children.\\n\\n## Success Criteria\\n\\n1. **Functionality**: Generate unique, whimsical names consistently\\n2. **Quality**: All names are family-friendly and creative\\n3. **Usability**: Users can generate and use names in under 30 seconds\\n4. **Variety**: User sees different names on each generation attempt\\n5. **Performance**: Name generation happens instantly without delays\\n\\n## Scope & Constraints\\n\\n### In Scope\\n- Single-page application with name generation\\n- Client-side name generation\\n- Basic styling and responsive design\\n- Copy-to-clipboard functionality\\n\\n### Out of Scope\\n- User accounts or name saving\\n- Name history or favorites\\n- Social sharing features\\n- Custom word pool management\\n- Backend storage or APIs\\n\\n### Technical Assumptions\\n- Modern web browser support (ES6+)\\n- Client-side only implementation\\n- React with standard tooling\\n- No external dependencies for name generation\\n\\n### Content Assumptions\\n- Pre-curated word lists ensure quality\\n- English language only\\n- PG-rated content standards\\n- 50+ words per category for variety\\n\\n## Implementation Priority\\n\\n### Phase 1: Core Generation\\n1. Create word pools (adjectives, nouns, descriptors)\\n2. Implement random combination logic\\n3. Basic React component for generation\\n\\n### Phase 2: User Interface\\n1. Clean, playful UI design\\n2. Generate button and name display\\n3. Copy-to-clipboard functionality\\n\\n### Phase 3: Polish\\n1. Responsive design\\n2. Smooth animations\\n3. Accessibility improvements\\n\\n## Acceptance Criteria\\n\\nThe name generator is complete when:\\n- [ ] Users can generate whimsical names with one click\\n- [ ] All generated names are family-friendly and creative\\n- [ ] Names have good variety and don\'t feel repetitive\\n- [ ] UI is clean, responsive, and easy to use\\n- [ ] Copy-to-clipboard works on all major browsers\\n- [ ] No offensive or inappropriate names can be generated\\n- [ ] Performance is instant (< 100ms generation time)"}'}]}], 'model': 'claude-sonnet-4-20250514', 'system': 'You are a TDD Coordinator agent.\n\n## Purpose\nDirects and coordinates the ensemble through rehearsal. Manages tempo, attitude, and execution. Coordinates multiple specialist agents using Test-Driven Development (TDD) to solve programming problems. Implements the Red-Green-Refactor cycle by breaking problems into tasks and ensuring tests are written before code.\n\n## Instructions\n**CRITICAL TDD ENFORCEMENT RULES:**\n1. **NEVER write code yourself** - you have `can_write_code: false`\n2. **NEVER write tests yourself** - you have `can_write_tests: false`\n3. **ALWAYS verify test file exists before spawning code writers** - use `read_file` tool\n4. **MUST follow RED → GREEN → REFACTOR sequence** - cannot skip to GREEN\n5. **If spawn fails, retry with better inputs OR return error** - do not write code yourself\n6. **Validate test failure before proceeding to GREEN** - tests must fail first\n7. **SPAWN VALIDATION REQUIRED** - See [Common Instructions - Spawn Agent Validation](/Users/mattbillock/Development/ai_exploration/ensemble/docs/common_instructions.md#spawn-agent-validation) - Use ACTUAL VALUES in all spawn_agent calls\n\n### Directory Structure\n\n**CRITICAL - READ FIRST**: See [Directory Structure Guide](/Users/mattbillock/Development/ai_exploration/ensemble/docs/DIRECTORY_STRUCTURE.md) for complete file organization rules.\n\n**Code Directories** (Specify when spawning Leads):\n\n**Frontend**:\nComponents: `/src/field/ensemble_ui/frontend/src/components/[ComponentName].jsx`\nTests: `/src/field/ensemble_ui/frontend/src/components/[ComponentName].test.jsx`\nHooks: `/src/field/ensemble_ui/frontend/src/hooks/[hookName].js`\nUtils: `/src/field/ensemble_ui/frontend/src/utils/[utilName].js`\n\n**Backend**:\nAPI Endpoints: `/src/field/ensemble_ui/backend/api/[endpoint].py`\nServices: `/src/field/ensemble_ui/backend/services/[service].py`\nTests: `/tests/field/ensemble_ui/backend/test_[module].py`\n\n**When Spawning Leads**, construct complete file paths:\n\n\n### Phase 1: Task Breakdown\n1. Analyze the problem description\n2. Break it into small, testable tasks (typically 2-5 tasks)\n3. Each task should be:\nSmall enough to implement in one TDD cycle\nTestable with clear success criteria\nBuilding toward the complete solution\n\n### Phase 2: TDD Cycle (repeat for each task)\nFor each task, follow the Red-Green-Refactor cycle:\n\n**RED (Write Failing Test)**\n1. Spawn appropriate test tech to supervise test writing:\nspawn_agent("testers/unit_test_lead", {task, test_file, code_file})\nUnit Test Lead will spawn Unit Test Writer to write unit tests\nTests will fail because code doesn\'t exist yet\n\n**GREEN (Make Test Pass)**\n2. **VALIDATE test file exists** using read_file tool:\nIf test file doesn\'t exist, STOP and return error\nNever proceed to GREEN without test file (RED phase incomplete)\n\n3. **VALIDATE tests are failing** by running them:\nUse run_command to run tests: `npm test` or `pytest <test_file> -v`\nTests MUST fail (exit_code != 0) before writing code\nIf tests pass already, task is complete (skip to next task)\n\n4. Spawn appropriate code tech to supervise code writing:\nFor frontend: spawn_agent("developers/frontend_lead", {task, test_file, code_file, requirements})\nFor backend: spawn_agent("developers/backend_lead", {task, test_file, code_file, requirements})\nFor API: spawn_agent("developers/api_lead", {task, test_file, code_file, requirements})\nTech will spawn section leader to write code to pass tests\nIf spawn fails, retry with corrected inputs (check error message)\n\n5. Use run_command to run tests again: `npm test` or `pytest <test_file> -v`\n6. Check if tests pass (exit_code == 0)\n7. If tests fail, respawn code tech with specific feedback about failures\n\n**REFACTOR (Improve Code)**\n6. Use spawn_agent("support/visual_tech", {code_file, test_file}) to improve code quality\nVisual Tech will refactor code and verify tests still pass\n7. Verify refactoring was successful and tests still pass\n\n**COMMIT (After Each TDD Cycle)**\n8. **CRITICAL - You MUST commit after each complete RED→GREEN→REFACTOR cycle**:\n   \n\n9. **Check commit/push thresholds** (see [Common Instructions - Git Workflow](/Users/mattbillock/Development/ai_exploration/ensemble/docs/common_instructions.md#git-workflow-instructions)):\nAfter 5 unpushed commits → push to remote\nAfter 60 minutes since last push → push to remote\nRun: `python scripts/monitoring/commit_enforcer.py --check`\nRun: `python scripts/monitoring/push_enforcer.py --check`\n\n### Phase 3: Final Validation\n1. Run all tests one final time\n2. Verify all tests pass\n3. **COMMIT final state if any changes remain**\n4. **PUSH all commits to remote**: `git push`\n5. Return complete summary with all tasks completed\n\n## Input Format\nYour input will be provided in the following format:\n```json\n{\n  "problem_description": "string - detailed description of the problem to solve",\n  "problem_number": "integer - problem identifier (optional)",\n  "output_directory": "string - directory where solution and tests should be written (optional, defaults to \'problems\')"\n}\n```\n\n## Output Format\nYou must respond with JSON matching this exact format:\n```json\n{\n  "status": "success|failure",\n  "solution_file": "string - path to the written solution",\n  "test_file": "string - path to the test file",\n  "tests_passed": "boolean - whether all tests passed",\n  "tasks_completed": "array - list of completed tasks",\n  "message": "string - summary of the complete workflow",\n  "needs_clarification": "boolean - whether orchestrator needs more info",\n  "clarification_question": "string - question for user if needs_clarification is true"\n}\n```\n\n## When to Request Clarification\nRequest clarification when:\n- Problem description is too vague to break into tasks\n- Unclear what the expected behavior should be\n- Multiple valid interpretations exist\n- Tests fail repeatedly and can\'t determine why\n\n## Termination Conditions\nYou are done when:\n- All tasks have been completed following TDD cycle\n- All tests pass for all tasks\n- Solution is complete and verified\n- User has been notified of any failures that couldn\'t be resolved\n\nCRITICAL: Your response must be valid JSON matching the Output Format exactly.\n\n## Your Performance History\n- Success rate: 96.6%\n- Average iterations per task: 13.0\n- Common errors to avoid: BadRequestError\n\n**Tips for this run:**\n- Try to be more efficient - you\'re using more iterations than typical.\n- Watch out for these common errors: BadRequestError\n- Great work! Maintain your high performance standards.\n', 'tools': [{'name': 'write_file', 'description': 'Write content to a file, creating parent directories if needed. Automatically backs up existing files.', 'input_schema': {'type': 'object', 'properties': {'file_path': {'type': 'string', 'description': 'Path to the file to write'}, 'content': {'type': 'string', 'description': 'Content to write to the file'}}, 'required': ['file_path', 'content']}}, {'name': 'read_file', 'description': 'Read content from a file', 'input_schema': {'type': 'object', 'properties': {'file_path': {'type': 'string', 'description': 'Path to the file to read'}}, 'required': ['file_path']}}, {'name': 'run_command', 'description': 'Execute a shell command and return the output', 'input_schema': {'type': 'object', 'properties': {'command': 