{"timestamp": "2026-01-14 21:05:57", "level": "DEBUG", "module": "anthropic._base_client", "message": "Request options: {'method': 'post', 'url': '/v1/messages', 'timeout': Timeout(connect=5.0, read=600, write=600, pool=600), 'files': None, 'idempotency_key': 'stainless-python-retry-896cd9f0-2338-4e43-b9bb-0554181504d3', 'json_data': {'max_tokens': 4096, 'messages': [{'role': 'user', 'content': 'Please complete the following task:\n\n{\n  "requirements_file": "/Users/mattbillock/Development/ai_exploration/ensemble/src/field/ensemble_ui/output/requirements.md",\n  "output_directory": "/Users/mattbillock/Development/ai_exploration/ensemble/src/field/ensemble_ui/output",\n  "project_name": "Whimsical Name Generator",\n  "continue_implementation": true,\n  "issue": "Previous implementation did not create visible implementation files in frontend/src directory. Need to complete actual implementation phase."\n}\n\nRemember to respond with valid JSON matching the expected output format.\n'}, {'role': 'assistant', 'content': [{'type': 'tool_use', 'id': 'toolu_01953rpwjmsyGQ3oEztsgU2z', 'name': 'read_file', 'input': {'file_path': '/Users/mattbillock/Development/ai_exploration/ensemble/src/field/ensemble_ui/output/requirements.md'}}]}, {'role': 'user', 'content': [{'type': 'tool_result', 'tool_use_id': 'toolu_01953rpwjmsyGQ3oEztsgU2z', 'content': '{"success": true, "content": "# Whimsical Name Generator - Requirements\\n\\n## Project Overview\\n\\n### Vision\\nCreate a fun, family-friendly whimsical name generator that produces unique, creative names to replace boring default names like \\"exec_dir_1\\". The generator should create names with personality and charm, such as \\"Whimsy Cloud Strider\\" or \\"Edge Citrusy Edge\\".\\n\\n### Core Problem\\nUsers are tired of boring, generic default names and want something fun and memorable that adds personality to their experience.\\n\\n### Solution\\nA whimsical name generator that combines creative adjectives, nouns, and descriptors to create unique, family-friendly names on demand.\\n\\n## Functional Requirements\\n\\n### Core Features\\n1. **Random Name Generation**\\n   - Generate unique whimsical names on demand\\n   - Combine multiple word categories (adjectives, nouns, descriptors)\\n   - Ensure family-friendly content only\\n\\n2. **Name Components**\\n   - Whimsical adjectives (Whimsy, Citrusy, Sparkly, Dreamy, etc.)\\n   - Nature/fantasy nouns (Cloud, Edge, Storm, Meadow, etc.)  \\n   - Action/descriptor words (Strider, Walker, Keeper, Singer, etc.)\\n\\n3. **User Interface**\\n   - Simple button to generate new name\\n   - Display current generated name prominently\\n   - Option to regenerate if user doesn\'t like current name\\n   - Copy-to-clipboard functionality\\n\\n4. **Name Quality**\\n   - All names must be family-friendly\\n   - Names should be memorable and fun\\n   - Avoid repetitive or boring combinations\\n   - 2-3 word combinations for good flow\\n\\n### Technical Requirements\\n1. **Frontend (React)**\\n   - Responsive design that works on all devices\\n   - Clean, playful UI design\\n   - Smooth animations for name generation\\n   - Accessible controls and text\\n\\n2. **Name Generation Logic**\\n   - Client-side generation for instant response\\n   - Large word pools to ensure variety\\n   - Smart combination logic to avoid awkward phrings\\n   - Randomization that feels truly random to users\\n\\n## Non-Functional Requirements\\n\\n### Performance\\n- Instant name generation (< 100ms)\\n- Lightweight implementation\\n- No external API dependencies needed\\n\\n### Usability\\n- One-click name generation\\n- Clear, readable typography\\n- Intuitive interface requiring no instructions\\n\\n### Content Standards\\n- All generated names must be appropriate for all ages\\n- No offensive, scary, or inappropriate word combinations\\n- Positive, uplifting tone in all generated content\\n\\n## User Stories\\n\\n1. **As a user**, I want to click a button and instantly get a fun, whimsical name so I can replace boring default names.\\n\\n2. **As a user**, I want to regenerate names until I find one I like so I can get the perfect name for my needs.\\n\\n3. **As a user**, I want to easily copy the generated name so I can use it elsewhere.\\n\\n4. **As a parent**, I want all generated names to be family-friendly so I can safely use this with my children.\\n\\n## Success Criteria\\n\\n1. **Functionality**: Generate unique, whimsical names consistently\\n2. **Quality**: All names are family-friendly and creative\\n3. **Usability**: Users can generate and use names in under 30 seconds\\n4. **Variety**: User sees different names on each generation attempt\\n5. **Performance**: Name generation happens instantly without delays\\n\\n## Scope & Constraints\\n\\n### In Scope\\n- Single-page application with name generation\\n- Client-side name generation\\n- Basic styling and responsive design\\n- Copy-to-clipboard functionality\\n\\n### Out of Scope\\n- User accounts or name saving\\n- Name history or favorites\\n- Social sharing features\\n- Custom word pool management\\n- Backend storage or APIs\\n\\n### Technical Assumptions\\n- Modern web browser support (ES6+)\\n- Client-side only implementation\\n- React with standard tooling\\n- No external dependencies for name generation\\n\\n### Content Assumptions\\n- Pre-curated word lists ensure quality\\n- English language only\\n- PG-rated content standards\\n- 50+ words per category for variety\\n\\n## Implementation Priority\\n\\n### Phase 1: Core Generation\\n1. Create word pools (adjectives, nouns, descriptors)\\n2. Implement random combination logic\\n3. Basic React component for generation\\n\\n### Phase 2: User Interface\\n1. Clean, playful UI design\\n2. Generate button and name display\\n3. Copy-to-clipboard functionality\\n\\n### Phase 3: Polish\\n1. Responsive design\\n2. Smooth animations\\n3. Accessibility improvements\\n\\n## Acceptance Criteria\\n\\nThe name generator is complete when:\\n- [ ] Users can generate whimsical names with one click\\n- [ ] All generated names are family-friendly and creative\\n- [ ] Names have good variety and don\'t feel repetitive\\n- [ ] UI is clean, responsive, and easy to use\\n- [ ] Copy-to-clipboard works on all major browsers\\n- [ ] No offensive or inappropriate names can be generated\\n- [ ] Performance is instant (< 100ms generation time)"}'}]}, {'role': 'assistant', 'content': [{'type': 'tool_use', 'id': 'toolu_015BWueKrWPZCMhtjrqaJxaC', 'name': 'project_tracking', 'input': {'action': 'get_summary', 'project_id': 'whimsical-name-generator'}}]}, {'role': 'user', 'content': [{'type': 'tool_result', 'tool_use_id': 'toolu_015BWueKrWPZCMhtjrqaJxaC', 'content': '{"success": true, "summary": {"error": "Project not found"}}'}]}, {'role': 'assistant', 'content': [{'type': 'tool_use', 'id': 'toolu_01VxRmxcZUgdriBtpC4mtpAX', 'name': 'git_status', 'input': {'include_history': True, 'history_count': 5}}]}, {'role': 'user', 'content': [{'type': 'tool_result', 'tool_use_id': 'toolu_01VxRmxcZUgdriBtpC4mtpAX', 'content': '{"success": true, "current_branch": "main", "changes": {"staged": [], "unstaged": [], "untracked": []}, "has_changes": false, "clean": true, "ahead": 2, "behind": 0, "last_commit": {"hash": "084a9e8f01f2a2a09a54d4047dbc9b9ac6db9bc9", "message": "Complete Achievement System Expansion milestone 1: foundation planning, architecture, and task breakdown for 100 DCI and NABBA themed achievements", "author": "Matt Billock", "when": "51 seconds ago"}, "history": [{"hash": "084a9e8f01f2a2a09a54d4047dbc9b9ac6db9bc9", "message": "Complete Achievement System Expansion milestone 1: foundation planning, architecture, and task breakdown for 100 DCI and NABBA themed achievements", "author": "Matt Billock", "when": "51 seconds ago"}, {"hash": "45b57283cde635a516d868d6bef8c96660a2376d", "message": "Complete milestone 1 planning: Whimsical Name Generator foundation architecture and task breakdown", "author": "Matt Billock", "when": "57 seconds ago"}, {"hash": "8d043ba9766733f56edb126e12ec12a5db158e6e", "message": "Add comprehensive agent hierarchy documentation and spawn permissions", "author": "Matt Billock", "when": "29 minutes ago"}, {"hash": "784833714132d5a2d9def39d867f3446186ee901", "message": "Add Best Practices and Anti-Patterns to all agent definitions", "author": "Matt Billock", "when": "32 minutes ago"}, {"hash": "ff7c891192831c1bdbe4f42984c309d09dee54cf", "message": "Complete architecture and task breakdown for Milestone 1 - Backend foundation with data models, API endpoints, and event integration", "author": "Matt Billock", "when": "88 minutes ago"}], "stash_count": 0}'}]}], 'model': 'claude-sonnet-4-20250514', 'system': 'You are a Development Manager agent.\n\n## Purpose\nDrives implementation from requirements through delivery. Breaks projects into milestones, identifies requirements gaps, drives architecture via System Architect and task breakdown via Coordinators, then coordinates with TDD Coordinator for implementation. Reports to Executive Director.\n\n## Instructions\nYou drive the show from concept through performance. Report to Executive Director, coordinate System Architect/Coordinators/TDD Coordinator.\n\n**CRITICAL RULES:**\n1. **NEVER write code yourself** - you lack can_write_code permission\n2. **If spawn_agent fails, STOP and return error** - DO NOT write code as fallback\n3. **Execute ALL steps sequentially** - don\'t stop after planning\n4. **Use EXACT agent paths** - see examples below\n5. **SPAWN VALIDATION REQUIRED** - See [Common Instructions - Spawn Agent Validation](/Users/mattbillock/Development/ai_exploration/ensemble/docs/common_instructions.md#spawn-agent-validation) - ALL spawn_agent calls MUST use ACTUAL VALUES, not placeholders\n\n### Directory Structure\n\n**CRITICAL - READ FIRST**: See [Directory Structure Guide](/Users/mattbillock/Development/ai_exploration/ensemble/docs/DIRECTORY_STRUCTURE.md) for complete file organization rules.\n\n**Your Write Locations** (Documentation Only):\n✓ `/src/field/ensemble_ui/output/architecture.md` - Architecture documents\n✓ `/src/field/ensemble_ui/output/milestone_plan.md` - Milestone plans\n✓ `/src/field/ensemble_ui/output/backend_tasks_m[N].md` - Backend task breakdowns\n✓ `/src/field/ensemble_ui/output/frontend_tasks_m[N].md` - Frontend task breakdowns\n✓ `/src/field/ensemble_ui/output/test_tasks_m[N].md` - Test task breakdowns\n\n**Code Directories** (Specify for Spawned Agents):\nWhen spawning TDD Coordinator or Coordinators, tell them WHERE to write code:\n\n**Frontend Code Paths**:\n\n\n**Backend Code Paths**:\n\n\n**Test Paths**:\n\n\n**When Spawning TDD Coordinator**, provide specific directories:\n\n\n### Process:\n\n**1. Read Requirements & Check Gaps**\nRead requirements file\n**BE DECISIVE**: Make reasonable technical decisions - ONLY ask if critical business decisions needed\nMissing: tech stack details → use modern defaults from requirements\nMissing: architecture patterns → use standard patterns (MVC, microservices, etc.)\nAmbiguous implementation → choose best practice approach\n**ONLY escalate when**: User must choose between major trade-offs (cost, security, compliance)\n\n**2. Create Milestones**\nBreak into logical, deliverable chunks\nEach milestone: objective, deliverables, acceptance criteria, dependencies\nWrite milestone plan document\n\n**3. Architecture - USE spawn_agent TOOL**\n**CRITICAL: Use spawn_agent tool**: spawn_agent("leadership/system_architect", {requirements_file})\nReview System Architect\'s architecture output\nIf major decisions need user input → escalate to Executive Director\n\n**4. Task Breakdown (for FIRST milestone) - USE spawn_agent TOOL**\n**CRITICAL: Actually use spawn_agent tool**, don\'t just write task files\nFor milestone 1, spawn each Coordinator using spawn_agent with proper inputs:\nspawn_agent("coordinators/backend_coordinator", {\n      "milestone": "description of milestone 1",\n      "architecture": "path/to/architecture.md",\n      "requirements": "path/to/requirements.md",\n      "output_file": "path/to/developer_tasks.md"\n    })\nspawn_agent("coordinators/test_coordinator", {\n      "milestone": "description of milestone 1",\n      "architecture": "path/to/architecture.md",\n      "requirements": "path/to/requirements.md",\n      "output_file": "path/to/test_tasks.md"\n    })\nspawn_agent("coordinators/frontend_coordinator", {similar inputs})\nReview each Coordinator\'s output for task breakdown\nConsolidate task lists, identify dependencies\n\n**5. Implementation (FIRST milestone) - USE spawn_agent TOOL**\n**CRITICAL: Use spawn_agent tool to spawn TDD Coordinator with EXACT path**\n**EXACT PATH**: spawn_agent("leadership/tdd_coordinator", {\n    "problem_description": "description of what to build",\n    "output_directory": "where to put code",\n    "test_directory": "where to put tests (optional)",\n    "requirements_file": "path/to/requirements.md (optional)"\n  })\nTDD Coordinator orchestrates Section Techs/Leaders via TDD\nMonitor TDD Coordinator\'s progress\n**If spawn fails, STOP and return error with details**\n\n**6. Verify Milestone Complete**\nAll tasks done? Tests passing? Quality acceptable? Docs written?\nIf yes → next milestone (repeat 4-6); if no → fix\n\n**7. Project Complete**\nAll milestones done → verify deliverables, run tests, check docs\nCommit all changes to version control (see Git Workflow below)\nReport to Executive Director with status: `success`\n\n### Git Workflow:\n**IMPORTANT**: Commit changes after completing each milestone and at project completion.\n\n**When to commit**:\nAfter milestone planning documents are written\nAfter architecture and task breakdown phases\nAfter each milestone implementation completes\nBefore reporting final completion to Executive Director\n\n**How to commit**:\n\n\n**Commit message guidelines**:\nBe specific: "Complete milestone 1: user authentication backend"\nNot generic: ❌ "update", "changes", "milestone done"\nMention milestone number or phase\nMinimum 10 characters\n\n**Example**:\n\n\n### Workflow Per Milestone:\n\n\n### Your Authority:\nDetermine milestone breakdown\nApprove task plans from Coordinators\nDecide when milestones complete\nEscalate to Executive Director when needed\n\n### Escalate to Executive Director When:\nRequirements gaps\nArchitecture needs user approval\nMajor blockers or scope changes\nQuality issues unresolvable\n\n## Input Format\nYour input will be provided in the following format:\n```json\n{\n  "requirements_file": "string - path to requirements document",\n  "output_directory": "string - where to create artifacts",\n  "project_name": "string - project name"\n}\n```\n\n## Output Format\nYou must respond with JSON matching this exact format:\n```json\n{\n  "status": "success|in_progress|needs_clarification|failed",\n  "phase": "string - milestones|architecture|task_breakdown|implementation|complete",\n  "milestones": "array of milestones if created",\n  "deliverables": "array of paths to created files",\n  "clarification_needed": "string - questions for Executive Director (optional)",\n  "message": "string - status summary",\n  "self_analysis": "string - REQUIRED: Your performance analysis (2-4 sentences)",\n  "performance_analysis": "string - REQUIRED: Analysis of System Architect, Coordinators, and TDD Coordinator performance (2-4 sentences)"\n}\n```\n\n## When to Request Clarification\nRequest clarification when:\n\n\n## Termination Conditions\nYou are done when:\n- All milestones completed, tests passing, documentation complete\n- Ready to report completion to Executive Director\n\nCRITICAL: Your response must be valid JSON matching the Output Format exactly.\n\n## Your Performance History\n- Success rate: 90.9%\n- Average iterations per task: 13.0\n- Common errors to avoid: BadRequestError\n\n**Tips for this run:**\n- Try to be more efficient - you\'re using more iterations than typical.\n- Watch out for these common errors: BadRequestError\n- Great work! Maintain your high performance standards.\n\n**Learnings from your recent runs:**\n- I successfully executed the complete planning workflow: read requirements, created milestone breakdown, spawned System Architect for architecture design, coordinated with all three Coordinators for ta...\n- I successfully executed the complete project lifecycle: read requirements, created milestone plan, spawned System Architect for architecture, coordinated with Backend/Frontend/Test Coordinators for ta...\n', 'tools': [{'name': 'write_file', 'description': 'Write content to a file, creating parent directories if needed. Automatically backs up existing files.', 'input_schema': {'type': 'object', 'properties': {'file_path': {'type': 'string', 'description': 'Path to the file to write'}, 'content': {'type': 'string', 'description': 'Content to write to the file'}}, 'required': ['file_path', 'content']}}, {'name': 'read_file', 'description': 'Read content from a file', 'input_schema': {'type': 'object', 'properties': {'file_path': {'type': 'string', 'description': 'Path to the file to read'}}, 'required': ['file_path']}}, {'name': 'run_command', 'description': 'Execute a shell command and return the output', 'input_schema': {'type': 'object', 'properties': {'command': {'type': 'string', 'description': 'The shell command to execute'}, 'working_directory': {'type': 'string', 'description': 'Optional working directory for command execution'}}, 'required': ['command']}}, {'name': 'git_commit', 'description': 'Commit changes to the git repository with a descriptive message', 'input_schema': {'type': 'object', 'properties': {'message': {'type': 'string', 'description': 'Commit message describing the changes'}, 'files': {'type': 'array', 'items': {'type': 'string'}, 'description': 'Optional list of specific files to commit. If not provided, commits all modified files.'}}, 'required': ['message']}}, {'name': 'git_branch', 'description': 'Create, switch, list,