{"timestamp": "2026-01-14 21:11:05", "level": "DEBUG", "module": "anthropic._base_client", "message": "Request options: {'method': 'post', 'url': '/v1/messages', 'timeout': Timeout(connect=5.0, read=600, write=600, pool=600), 'files': None, 'idempotency_key': 'stainless-python-retry-a69b068d-1681-42d0-b941-d2e17aca8a92', 'json_data': {'max_tokens': 4096, 'messages': [{'role': 'user', 'content': 'Please complete the following task:\n\n{\n  "task": "Create both test file and implementation file for name generation",\n  "test_file": "/Users/mattbillock/Development/ai_exploration/ensemble/src/field/ensemble_ui/frontend/src/__tests__/nameGenerator.test.js",\n  "code_file": "/Users/mattbillock/Development/ai_exploration/ensemble/src/field/ensemble_ui/frontend/src/utils/nameGenerator.js",\n  "action": "create_both_files",\n  "requirements": "Create test file first with comprehensive tests for: 1) Word arrays contain 50+ family-friendly words each (adjectives, nouns, descriptors), 2) generateName() function returns string with 2-3 words, 3) Generated names are family-friendly, 4) Function produces variety in outputs. Then create minimal implementation to pass tests.",\n  "test_driven_development": true\n}\n\nRemember to respond with valid JSON matching the expected output format.\n'}, {'role': 'assistant', 'content': [{'type': 'tool_use', 'id': 'toolu_016Jdm6EC3Er7wkBMuqzEK7D', 'name': 'write_file', 'input': {'file_path': '/Users/mattbillock/Development/ai_exploration/ensemble/src/field/ensemble_ui/frontend/src/__tests__/nameGenerator.test.js', 'content': "import { generateName, adjectives, nouns, descriptors } from '../utils/nameGenerator';\n\ndescribe('nameGenerator', () => {\n  describe('word arrays', () => {\n    test('adjectives array contains at least 50 family-friendly words', () => {\n      expect(adjectives).toBeDefined();\n      expect(Array.isArray(adjectives)).toBe(true);\n      expect(adjectives.length).toBeGreaterThanOrEqual(50);\n      \n      // Check for family-friendly content (no inappropriate words)\n      const inappropriateWords = ['damn', 'hell', 'stupid', 'dumb', 'crazy', 'insane'];\n      adjectives.forEach(word => {\n        expect(inappropriateWords.some(bad => word.toLowerCase().includes(bad))).toBe(false);\n        expect(typeof word).toBe('string');\n        expect(word.length).toBeGreaterThan(0);\n      });\n    });\n\n    test('nouns array contains at least 50 family-friendly words', () => {\n      expect(nouns).toBeDefined();\n      expect(Array.isArray(nouns)).toBe(true);\n      expect(nouns.length).toBeGreaterThanOrEqual(50);\n      \n      // Check for family-friendly content\n      const inappropriateWords = ['weapon', 'gun', 'knife', 'violence'];\n      nouns.forEach(word => {\n        expect(inappropriateWords.some(bad => word.toLowerCase().includes(bad))).toBe(false);\n        expect(typeof word).toBe('string');\n        expect(word.length).toBeGreaterThan(0);\n      });\n    });\n\n    test('descriptors array contains at least 50 family-friendly words', () => {\n      expect(descriptors).toBeDefined();\n      expect(Array.isArray(descriptors)).toBe(true);\n      expect(descriptors.length).toBeGreaterThanOrEqual(50);\n      \n      // Check for family-friendly content\n      const inappropriateWords = ['ugly', 'disgusting', 'horrible', 'awful'];\n      descriptors.forEach(word => {\n        expect(inappropriateWords.some(bad => word.toLowerCase().includes(bad))).toBe(false);\n        expect(typeof word).toBe('string');\n        expect(word.length).toBeGreaterThan(0);\n      });\n    });\n  });\n\n  describe('generateName function', () => {\n    test('returns a string', () => {\n      const name = generateName();\n      expect(typeof name).toBe('string');\n      expect(name.length).toBeGreaterThan(0);\n    });\n\n    test('returns 2-3 words separated by spaces', () => {\n      const name = generateName();\n      const words = name.trim().split(/\\s+/);\n      expect(words.length).toBeGreaterThanOrEqual(2);\n      expect(words.length).toBeLessThanOrEqual(3);\n      \n      // Each word should be non-empty\n      words.forEach(word => {\n        expect(word.length).toBeGreaterThan(0);\n      });\n    });\n\n    test('generates family-friendly names', () => {\n      // Generate multiple names to test\n      for (let i = 0; i < 20; i++) {\n        const name = generateName();\n        const inappropriateWords = ['damn', 'hell', 'stupid', 'dumb', 'weapon', 'gun', 'ugly'];\n        \n        inappropriateWords.forEach(badWord => {\n          expect(name.toLowerCase().includes(badWord)).toBe(false);\n        });\n      }\n    });\n\n    test('produces variety in outputs', () => {\n      const names = new Set();\n      const iterations = 50;\n      \n      for (let i = 0; i < iterations; i++) {\n        names.add(generateName());\n      }\n      \n      // Should have at least 80% unique names (allowing for some duplicates)\n      expect(names.size).toBeGreaterThan(iterations * 0.8);\n    });\n\n    test('uses words from the provided arrays', () => {\n      const name = generateName();\n      const words = name.toLowerCase().split(/\\s+/);\n      const allWords = [...adjectives, ...nouns, ...descriptors].map(w => w.toLowerCase());\n      \n      // At least one word should come from our arrays\n      const hasWordFromArrays = words.some(word => allWords.includes(word));\n      expect(hasWordFromArrays).toBe(true);\n    });\n\n    test('capitalizes first letter of each word', () => {\n      const name = generateName();\n      const words = name.split(/\\s+/);\n      \n      words.forEach(word => {\n        expect(word.charAt(0)).toBe(word.charAt(0).toUpperCase());\n      });\n    });\n  });\n});"}}]}, {'role': 'user', 'content': [{'type': 'tool_result', 'tool_use_id': 'toolu_016Jdm6EC3Er7wkBMuqzEK7D', 'content': '{"success": false, "error": "ROGUE AGENT DETECTED: Agent \'Executive Director\' attempted to write test file \'/Users/mattbillock/Development/ai_exploration/ensemble/src/field/ensemble_ui/frontend/src/__tests__/nameGenerator.test.js\' but lacks can_write_tests permission. This agent is a supervisor/coordinator and should delegate to test writers."}'}]}], 'model': 'claude-sonnet-4-20250514', 'system': 'You are a Frontend Developer agent.\n\n## Purpose\nFrontend code writer. Provides the bright, prominent frontend work. Writes React/JavaScript code for UI components, pages, and frontend logic. Focused on making tests pass and delivering clean, functional components.\n\n## Instructions\nYou write React components that pass existing tests. Focus on clean, minimal code.\n\n**JSON OUTPUT REQUIRED**: See [Common Instructions - JSON Output Format](/Users/mattbillock/Development/ai_exploration/ensemble/docs/common_instructions.md#json-output-format-requirement) - You MUST return valid JSON matching the Output Format schema above.\n\n### Process:\n\n**BE DECISIVE**: Make reasonable UI implementation choices. ONLY ask for clarification if user interaction is genuinely unclear.\n\n**Default Implementation Choices**:\n**Components**: Functional components with hooks\n**Styling**: Tailwind classes or CSS modules (match project)\n**State**: useState for local, lift up when shared\n**Forms**: Controlled components with validation\n**Events**: onClick, onChange, onSubmit with clear handlers\n**Accessibility**: Semantic HTML (button not div), ARIA when needed\n\n**DO NOT ask for clarification about**:\nComponent structure (functional with hooks)\nStyling approach (Tailwind or CSS modules)\nEvent naming (handleClick, handleSubmit)\nProp naming (camelCase, descriptive)\nFile organization (one component per file)\n\n**1. Read Tests**\nRead test_file to understand requirements\nIdentify what component structure, props, state, and behavior are expected\nNote any user interactions that need handling\nIdentify edge cases to handle\n\n**2. Plan Component**\nDetermine component structure\nIdentify required props and state\nPlan event handlers\nConsider styling approach (Tailwind, CSS modules, etc.)\n\n**3. Write Minimal Code**\nImport necessary dependencies (React, useState, etc.)\nCreate functional component with proper props\nImplement state management if needed\nAdd event handlers for user interactions\nReturn JSX matching test expectations\n**CRITICAL**: Write ONLY enough code to pass tests - no extra features\n\n**4. Validate**\nCheck syntax is valid\nEnsure imports are correct\nVerify component exports properly\nUse write_file to save component\n\n**5. Commit Changes**\nAfter component is written and validated\nUse git_commit with descriptive message\nSee Git Workflow section below\n\n### Git Workflow:\nAfter successfully implementing and testing your component, commit the changes:\n\n\n\n**Commit message examples**:\n"Implement LoginForm component with validation"\n"Add UserProfile component with avatar display"\n"Implement Dashboard with data visualization"\n\n**When to commit**:\nAfter writing component and verifying it\'s valid\nBefore returning final status\n\n### React Best Practices:\nUse functional components with hooks\nDestructure props for clarity\nUse descriptive variable names\nKeep components focused (single responsibility)\nExtract reusable logic to custom hooks if appropriate\nUse prop-types or TypeScript if project uses them\nEnsure accessibility (semantic HTML, ARIA when needed)\n\n### Code Style:\nClear, readable code\nProper indentation\nMeaningful variable/function names\nComments only where logic isn\'t self-evident\nFollow project\'s existing style patterns\n\n### Example Component Structure:\n\n## Input Format\nYour input will be provided in the following format:\n```json\n{\n  "task": "string - description of component/page to build",\n  "test_file": "string - path to test file that code must pass",\n  "code_file": "string - path where component should be written",\n  "requirements": "string - path to requirements document (optional)",\n  "related_tasks": "string - info about related components/APIs (optional)"\n}\n```\n\n## Output Format\nYou must respond with JSON matching this exact format:\n```json\n{\n  "status": "success|failure",\n  "code_file": "string - path to written component",\n  "message": "string - summary of what was implemented",\n  "needs_clarification": "boolean - whether agent needs more info",\n  "clarification_question": "string - question if needs_clarification is true"\n}\n```\n\n## When to Request Clarification\nRequest clarification when:\n- **User interaction genuinely ambiguous** (e.g., "click button" but what happens?)\n- **Tests contradict each other** (one expects X, another expects Y)\n- **Required behavior unclear AND tests don\'t specify** (e.g., form validation rules)\n- **Test file missing or corrupted** (can\'t proceed without tests in TDD)\n- **NOT for**: styling details, component structure, naming conventions, standard patterns\n\n## Termination Conditions\nYou are done when:\n- Code has been written and saved to the output file\n- Code runs without syntax errors\n- Code passes all tests\n- Component is properly structured and follows React best practices\n- Agent has validated the solution addresses the requirements\n\nCRITICAL: Your response must be valid JSON matching the Output Format exactly.\n\n## Your Performance History\n- Success rate: 100.0%\n- Average iterations per task: 3.3\n\n**Tips for this run:**\n- Great work! Maintain your high performance standards.\n', 'tools': [{'name': 'write_file', 'description': 'Write content to a file, creating parent directories if needed. Automatically backs up existing files.', 'input_schema': {'type': 'object', 'properties': {'file_path': {'type': 'string', 'description': 'Path to the file to write'}, 'content': {'type': 'string', 'description': 'Content to write to the file'}}, 'required': ['file_path', 'content']}}, {'name': 'read_file', 'description': 'Read content from a file', 'input_schema': {'type': 'object', 'properties': {'file_path': {'type